{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c3c5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b42c-6247-7d31-b9d8-d87c5b1f64f4"},"sequence":61,"recorded_at":1780531400000117,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"0dc60d48-0449-4263-a4d2-db59edd40fb4","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"0dc60d48-0449-4263-a4d2-db59edd40fb4","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"0dc60d48-0449-4263-a4d2-db59edd40fb4"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b42c-928d-7991-ae1c-525ab65bf54b"},"task_id":"01a0b42c-928d-7991-ae1c-525ab65bf54b","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b42c-928d-7991-ae1c-525ab65bf54b","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-32ypr2/TASK-260830-32ypr2_rework-rev3.md`.\n1|THIS BRIEF SUPERSEDES EVERY EARLIER PRECONDITION ON TASK-260830-32ypr2, including TASK-260830-32ypr2_rework-rev2.md. Do exactly what is written here.\n2|Rework run for TASK-260830-32ypr2, the FINAL leaf of STORY-260830-1cyj0q. Story_final revision 2 was reviewed by RUN-260918-a4ffef (claude-opus-5 max) and routed CHANGES REQUESTED: one P1, one P2, a P3 list. Read TASK-260830-32ypr2_review-verdict-rev2.md and TASK-260830-32ypr2_review-evidence-rev2.tar.gz before touching anything. Every rev1 finding is closed AT THE VECTOR IT NAMED and your evidence reproduces on the exact tree — the reviewer says so in its Section 0. That is also the problem, and this is the third round in which it is the problem: what fails is the CLASS that both the rev1 verdict and the rev2 brief told this leaf to close.\n3|The projection still reads the record envelope through a SECOND, LENIENT decoder after the strict gate, and that decoder diverges from the admitted member map on case-folded member names. Through that divergence, on the pristine candidate and admitted by your own committed suite: a foreign instruction reaches the effective snapshot with `authority=high`; an unknown record is coerced into `user_message`; a foreign encrypted `reasoning/summary` is promoted to `reasoning_summary`; sealed content and the evidence identity are taken from a member the record does not claim; and a record is re-attributed to `main`. Every one of those is stamped `capture_status: exact`. Those five outcomes are precisely the invariants this leaf exists to guarantee, and the tree, the TRACEABILITY, the LOGBOOK and the results all state in so many words that they cannot happen.\n4|So the instruction this round is not \"fix the class\" — that has not worked twice. It is mechanical, and the reviewer has already proven the target shape green:\n5|1. DELETE the second decoder from the projection path. Read the six claimed envelope members from the STRICT map only. The reviewer's `logs/fixprobe-strict-map-envelope.log` contains the 12-line shape that does this and is proven green on your tree — use it. There must be no lenient re-read of the envelope anywhere after the strict gate; grep your own package for a second decode of the same bytes and remove every one.\n6|2. Add one committed row per AC-relevant alias axis — kind, origin/authority, protection/promotion, body/content, evidence identity, actor — plus a narrowing mutant that restores the case-folded read for EXACTLY ONE member. That narrowing must die; if it survives, the class is still open and you should say so rather than hand off.\n7|3. Correct the five prose sites that currently assert the opposite of what the tree does: `native.go`, TRACEABILITY lines 34, 65 and 96, the README, the LOGBOOK REV2 entry (append a correction, do not rewrite history) and the results.\n8|4. P2-d: one positive `reasoning_summary` row (kind, `internal`, content, `exact`) with the routing swap as its narrowing.\n9|5. P3-m..t: capture-status assertions per kind; pin or drop last-wins; pin the external actor kind; the unknown-type-without-body row; state or refuse `text:null`; relabel `N-pending-aborted` and the shared-site `N-strict-*` rows; fix the LOGBOOK REV2 sentence.\n10|6. Re-run the battery twice on the final tree, re-run tracecheck, report the ratio you MEASURE, and keep the candidate UNCOMMITTED.\n11|Procedure: this is the FINAL leaf, so internal/traceability is yours — the adopted registry is `ownership.v0.7.0.json`, the pin must be re-derived from the registry as it stands in your candidate, and the README measured-coverage subsection must equal what tracecheck prints and still pass the landed `readme_coverage_pin_test.go`. Your Story branch descends from c3aae73; the sibling Story STORY-260830-ptxkqe may land first, and if origin/main moves you must run `task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-32ypr2`, audit every path in `git diff --name-only c3aae73 <new base>` that also appears in your `git status`, keep README and LOGBOOK edits additive on the NEW content, and MERGE the ownership registry rather than replacing it. Never commit on the Story branch, never edit `.task-board` directly, never self-accept. Run your own package tests and the three harnesses BEFORE handoff, then the full configured suite once (30 commands; read the count from the candidate config). Update the results with a finding-by-finding table (finding -> change -> the test that fails without it -> evidence path), update the conformance matrix and the evidence archive (a real gzip archive, one raw log per plant with its subprocess exit, PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1), re-complete the checklist, then `task-board handoff TASK-260830-32ypr2 --role developer` so revision 3 is constructed, and exit promptly. Hand off no later than 2.5 hours in.\n12|PARTIAL-ATTEMPT RECOVERY: if a previous attempt died mid-way, the Story worktree still carries its partial edits — start with `git -C .temp/STORY-260830-1cyj0q/worktree status --short` and `git diff`, state what you inherited, and verify it against this brief instead of assuming it is correct.\n13|Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: muse-spark max. The same claude-opus-5 max reviewer contract applies to revision 3.","final_result":true}}}
