{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c507","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b42c-6247-7d31-b9d8-d87c5b1f64f4"},"sequence":222,"recorded_at":1780531400000439,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"0dc60d48-0449-4263-a4d2-db59edd40fb4","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"0dc60d48-0449-4263-a4d2-db59edd40fb4","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"0dc60d48-0449-4263-a4d2-db59edd40fb4"},"call_id":"call_01a0b42d3c2b74ff95e9c5b1a5f1828b","text":"Read text file `.temp/TASK-260830-32ypr2/rev2-review/TASK-260830-32ypr2_review-verdict-rev2.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-32ypr2 — Review verdict, Change Request revision 2\n2|\n3|Reviewer run: RUN-260918-a4ffef (claude-opus-5 max, reviewer/reviewer).\n4|Change Request: `CR-TASK-260830-32ypr2-2` revision 2 (story_final), base\n5|`c3aae73df906df1b5aa962c7bc3c16437dd920fa` (= `origin/main`, re-fetched at\n6|review start, unmoved), candidate tree\n7|`5832072adaf91325edff9ee636a8b93aa2cc2d99` (65 paths; patch sha256\n8|`1562a1c2b703d19124e760aa14eb022a498208854861d72bfabb594366bf4402`, verified\n9|byte-equal to `git diff c3aae73 5832072`). The live Story worktree's\n10|temp-index tree OID (`git add -A` into a scratch index) equalled `5832072…`\n11|before this review; `git status` stayed ` M LOGBOOK.md`, ` M README.md`,\n12|` M internal/clonesnap/{TRACEABILITY.md,project.go}`,\n13|` M internal/traceability/{6 files}`, `?? internal/cloneproject/` throughout.\n14|Worktree, index, branch and HEAD were never touched. Authority:\n15|`internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md` §13.14.1 (10331–10546; the fidelity\n16|paragraph at 10388–10394), §10.2, §7.8, §1.6 (line 324).\n17|\n18|Method: isolated immutable copies of the exact candidate tree\n19|(`git archive 5832072…` → `.temp/TASK-260830-32ypr2/rev2-review/{candidate,\n20|pristine,battery,fixprobe,plantprobe}`; the tracked `.task-board` dropped\n21|from the copies and re-materialized only for the `specpin` board-scope\n22|test); `diff -rq` clean between `battery` and `candidate` after every\n23|harness run; `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1` on every harness, zero\n24|`__pycache__`/`.pyc` after the runs. Every probe named below was executed on\n25|the candidate copy; logs are in `TASK-260830-32ypr2_review-evidence-rev2.tar.gz`.\n26|\n27|## Verdict: CHANGES REQUESTED → `to-dev`\n28|\n29|One P1, one P2, a P3 list. Every rev1 finding is closed at the vector it\n30|named and the producer's evidence reproduces on the exact tree (Section 0).\n31|What fails is the CLASS the rev1 verdict and the cr2 brief both told this\n32|leaf to close: the projection still reads the record envelope through a\n33|second, lenient decoder after the strict gate, and that decoder diverges\n34|from the admitted member map on case-folded member names. Through that\n35|divergence a foreign instruction reaches the effective snapshot with\n36|`authority=high`, an unknown record is coerced into `user_message`, a\n37|foreign encrypted `reasoning/summary` is promoted to `reasoning_summary`,\n38|sealed content and the evidence identity come from a member the record does\n39|not claim, and a record is re-attributed to `main` — all stamped\n40|`capture_status: exact`, all on the pristine candidate, all admitted by the\n41|committed suite. The tree, the TRACEABILITY, the LOGBOOK and the results\n42|state in so many words that this cannot happen.\n43|\n44|## Section 0 — rev1 rework verification (RUN-260918-320878 findings)\n45|\n46|| Finding | Grade | Evidence |\n47||---|---|---|\n48|| P1-a strict-decode fork (lone surrogate / duplicate member rewritten, stamped `exact`) | CLOSED AT THE VECTORS, NOT THE CLASS — see P1-b | `strictMembers` delegates to `environ.DecodeStrictObject` at both frame sites (`native.go:71-80`, `:94`, `:254`); rows `lone_surrogate_text`, `lone_surrogate_envelope`, `duplicate_envelope_member`, `duplicate_body_member` refuse with the literal fault (`pkg-cloneproject-v.log`); narrowings `N-strict-*` KILLED 2/2 in my runs. The envelope is then re-read by `json.NewDecoder(...).Decode(&envelope)` (`native.go:108-111`) — a second decoder whose case-insensitive field matching the strict map does not share (P1-b, `logs/probe-case-alias.log`). |\n49|| P2-a inherited advisories dropped; false prose in `clonesnap/project.go:41-43`, `clonesnap/TRACEABILITY.md:132-147` | CLOSED | One decision line per group (1, 2, 3, 5, 6, 7b deferred with owners; 4 closed as a stated bound; 7a closed by the strict rows; 7c bound) in results + matrix D; both prose sites rewritten to what the tree does and every name they cite exists (`fidelityProfiles` `operations.go:535`, `TestValueVocabulariesMatchSpec`, `TestProjectAdmitsStableEveryProfile`, `TestProjectRefusesUnknownProfile`, `excludedClass`, `alwaysExcludedClass`, `measurePost` unconditional at `capture.go:314`). |\n50|| P2-b `7.8#1` discharged by a test constructing no frame | CLOSED | Registry `7.8#1` → `session-adapter-frame-bound` (production `sessadapter/protocol.go DecodeRequestFrame`, `MaxFrameBytes = 8<<20` at :34; tests `TestDecodeRequestFrameRefusesOversizeFrame` builds a > 8 MiB frame and asserts `exceeds the 8 MiB bound`, `TestFrameBoundEdges` witnesses exact/one-over on request, success and failure gates — `envelope_test.go:127,144`); `clone-projection-fidelity` removed from the 7.8 binding; `--section 7.8` admitted (`logs/section-7.8.log`). |\n51|| P2-c `bodyUint53` fork admitting `\"5\"` | CLOSED | `environ.CheckUint53Bounds(members[name], 0, maxUint53)` at `native.go:302`; envelope version through the same gate at `:112`; rows `string_usage_number`, `string_envelope_version`; my PB3 sweep (`1.0`, `1e0`, `-0`, `01`, `true`, `[1]`) refuses every literal but `1` (`logs/probe-value-shapes.log`). |\n52|| P3-a..h, i, j, k, l | CLOSED (a, b, d, e, f, g, h rows + narrowings; i and l pinned as bounds; j union of 11 cases with `10.2#2` gaining `localstore-immutable-blob-install`; k relabelled) | Rows present and PASS; `N-actors-sort`, `N-reasoning-encrypted-signed`, `N-reasoning-signed-encrypted`, `N-trailing-admitted`, `N-protected-tools-skip`, `N-result-status-pending`, `N-size-verify`, `N-unknown-protected-body` KILLED 2/2. P3-c stated as a bound (measured again below: `R2-native-type-width-513` SURVIVED 2/2, within the stated bound). |\n53|| Battery / tracecheck / digest / suite | REPRODUCED | 65-row battery: 64 KILLED + `C-doc-comment` SURVIVED, 2/2, one raw log per plant per run (`mutants/producer-run{1,2}/`, `producer-run{1,2}-battery.log`); `tracecheck` byte-equal to the quoted lines; digest re-derived by zeroing the pin → `4bd01143702d17bc05f187a14312cb868b85276b0f0b6d015c351929eae9bfc0` = pinned (`logs/digest-rederivation.log`); package suite 80 PASS / 0 FAIL (`logs/pkg-cloneproject-v.log`). |\n54|\n55|## Findings\n56|\n57|### P1 — the strict gate admits, a second decoder guesses, and `exact` is stamped\n58|\n59|**P1-b `parseNativeLine` re-reads the envelope through `encoding/json`\n60|struct decoding after the strict map admitted it; case-folded member\n61|aliases change the projected kind, origin, authority, content, evidence\n62|identity and attribution.** `environ.DecodeStrictObject` compares member\n63|names exactly (`Origin` and `origin` are distinct keys, so no duplicate\n64|fault), but the struct decode at `internal/cloneproject/native.go:108-111`\n65|matches field names case-insensitively and takes the LAST match in document\n66|order. The comment above it (`:104-107`, \"the struct read cannot diverge\n67|from the admitted members\") and the `strictMembers` comment (`:66-70`,\n68|\"later reads of the admitted bytes are exact because the rewriting and\n69|guessing shapes never reach them\") are false. Pristine candidate, real\n70|`clonesnap.Capture` → `Normalize` path, every row ADMITTED with\n71|`capture_status=exact` (`logs/probe-case-alias.log`):\n72|\n73|| Probe | Record (one extra envelope member) | Projected |\n74||---|---|---|\n75|| PA1 | `\"native_type\":\"frobnicate\",\"NATIVE_TYPE\":\"message/user\"` | `user_message`, `public`, evidence `native_type=\"message/user\"` — an unknown record coerced into a known kind (AC 1: \"never guessed, coerced into a neighbouring kind\") |\n76|| PA2 | same alias placed BEFORE `native_type` | `opaque_event` — the outcome depends on member order, i.e. on a member the projection does not claim |\n77|| PA3 | `instruction/snapshot`, `\"origin\":\"foreign\",\"Origin\":\"native\"`, body `authority:high` | `Instruction={Found:true Authority:high Directives:[DROP-EVERYTHING]}`, payload `authority:high` — the AC-named gate (\"an instruction carried in a foreign record cannot change the projected session's effective instruction snapshot or authority\") defeated |\n78|| PA4 | `\"body\":{\"text\":\"declared\"},\"Body\":{\"text\":\"smuggled\"}` | content block `smuggled` — sealed content from a member the record does not claim |\n79|| PA5 | `\"native_event_id\":\"evt-a5\",\"Native_Event_Id\":\"evt-forged\"` | evidence `native_event_id=\"evt-forged\"` — the evidence identity rewritten |\n80|| PA6 | `reasoning/summary`, `\"origin\":\"foreign\",\"protection\":\"encrypted\",\"Protection\":\"none\"`, plaintext body | `reasoning_summary`, `internal`, content projected, no reason code — a record whose `protection` member says `encrypted` is promoted to `reasoning_summary` (AC 2: \"never ... promoted to reasoning_summary\") |\n81|| PA7 | `\"actor\":\"subagent:ghost\",\"Actor\":\"main\"` | attributed to `main` (pristine without the alias refuses `subagent:ghost` as unmapped) |\n82|| PA8 | control: `\"extra\":true` | admitted as an unclaimed extra — the stated \"envelope extras unclaimed\" bound covers this, not PA1–PA7 |\n83|\n84|Why P1, not P2: (a) it is the same class the Story has been rejected for\n85|three times (decode-and-continue that diverges from the gate — numbers,\n86|extension values, text) and that the cr2 brief told this leaf to close \"at\n87|the entry, not the two witnessed vectors\"; the rework closed the two\n88|vectors and left the second decoder in place, now documented as unable to\n89|diverge. (b) It defeats gates the AC names by sentence (unknown → opaque;\n90|foreign instruction low-authority; foreign encrypted reasoning never\n91|promoted) and rewrites the evidence identity and content while stamping\n92|`exact`, which is exactly the P1-a shape. (c) Shipped prose asserts the\n93|property in five places: `native.go:66-70,104-107`,\n94|`internal/cloneproject/TRACEABILITY.md:34` (\"before any member is read\"),\n95|`:65` (\"never dropped, guessed, or re-typed\"), `:96` (\"never rewritten\"),\n96|README:2458 (\"low-authority history that never changes the effective\n97|instruction snapshot\"), LOGBOOK REV2 line (\"the later struct read is\n98|exact because the rewriting/guessing shapes never pass the gate\"), results\n99|finding table row 1 (same sentence). The stated bound \"envelope extras\n100|unclaimed\" does not cover an extra that overrides a claimed member's value.\n101|\n102|The fix is not a forced fit. In a throwaway copy\n103|(`logs/fixprobe-strict-map-envelope.log`) I replaced the struct decode with\n104|reads of the six claimed members from the strict map (`json.Unmarshal(\n105|members[\"native_event_id\"], &envelope.NativeEventID)` … and\n106|`envelope.Body = members[\"body\"]`; 12 lines, no second decoder). The\n107|committed suite stays green (80/80), and under the fix PA1 → `opaque_event\n108|frobnicate`, PA3 → `Found:false`, payload `authority:low`, PA4 → content\n109|`declared`, PA5 → `evt-a5`, PA6 → refused (`body carries unknown member\n110|\"text\"`), PA7 → refused (`subagent:ghost` unmapped), PA8 still admitted.\n111|Ship: the strict-map read (or `environ.CheckStringBounds(members[...],\n112|1, 512)` for the bounded members, which also removes the `StringLength`\n113|double-call), one committed row per alias axis that matters to the AC\n114|(native_type → kind; origin → effective snapshot and authority; protection\n115|→ promotion; body → content; native_event_id → evidence identity; actor →\n116|attribution), and a narrowing that re-introduces the case-folded read for\n117|exactly one member. Then correct the five prose sites.\n118|\n119|### P2 — an emitted kind with no committed row\n120|\n121|**P2-d `reasoning_summary` (unprotected `reasoning/summary`) has no positive\n122|test; a kind/visibility swap survives the whole suite.**\n123|`R5-reasoning-summary-routed-public` (`dispatch.go:180-182`: `default:`\n124|arm routed to `user_message`/`public`) SURVIVED 2/2 against `-run\n125|TestNormalize` (`mutants/reviewer-run{1,2}/R5-*.log`). `grep\n126|'reasoning/summary\\|reasoning_summary' *_test.go` finds only the\n127|promotion-negative assertion and the protected-plaintext refusal row: no\n128|test drives an unprotected `reasoning/summary` record. TRACEABILITY's\n129|fact-registry table (`:47`) and the results' \"registries cover exactly the\n130|ten emitted kinds\" therefore describe a row nothing executes, and a\n131|reasoning summary sealed with `public` visibility would pass review. One\n132|positive row (kind `reasoning_summary`, visibility `internal`, content\n133|block, `exact`) and the swap as its narrowing.\n134|\n135|### P3 — unpinned members and labels (production correct in each case; each plant SURVIVED 2/2 against the whole committed suite, `mutants/reviewer-run{1,2}/`)\n136|\n137|- **P3-m capture status is pinned on the opaque row only.**\n138|  `R4-capture-status-partial-messages` (`dispatch.go:389`: `partial` for\n139|  exactly `message/user`) SURVIVED 2/2; only\n140|  `TestNormalizeUnknownRecordBecomesOpaqueEvent` asserts `exact`. Assert the\n141|  status on at least one row per emitted kind, or on every event in\n142|  `TestNormalizeSealsSessionShape`.\n143|- **P3-n fold order is a doc claim.** `R6-first-native-instruction-wins`\n144|  (`tools.go:171`) SURVIVED 2/2; no test carries two native instructions.\n145|  Either pin last-wins with two native records or drop the sentence.\n146|- **P3-o external actor kind unpinned.** `R7-external-actor-kind-subagent`\n147|  (`dispatch.go:417`) SURVIVED 2/2; `TestNormalizeActorOrderIsDeterministic`\n148|  references `external` but asserts nothing about its sealed kind.\n149|- **P3-p required-member gate pinned by message, on a known type only.**\n150|  `R1-required-member-body-dropped` (`native.go:98`, `body` removed from the\n151|  list) KILLED 2/2 — but only because `missing_envelope_member` (a\n152|  `message/user` fixture) then refuses with a different fragment at the body\n153|  decode. Under the plant an unknown type without a body is ADMITTED as\n154|  `opaque_event` (`logs/under-mutant-R1.log`). Add the unknown-type row.\n155|- **P3-q `\"text\":null` seals as empty inline content, `exact`** (PB1,\n156|  `logs/probe-value-shapes.log`): `json.Unmarshal(null, &string)` leaves the\n157|  string empty. `directives:null` was stated as a bound; `text:null` was not.\n158|  State it or refuse it (`ciphertext:null` is harmless: never read).\n159|- **P3-r `N-pending-aborted` is an add-arm plant on an unreachable arm.**\n160|  `Normalize` passes `nil` live work orders (`normalize.go:176`), so the\n161|  `continue` at `tools.go:136` cannot be measured from the entry; the plant\n162|  appends `call-7` explicitly. Matrix rows 13/17 call it a \"killer\"\n163|  narrowing. Label it (the matrix D bound already says nothing captured can\n164|  pend). Same for the results' \"No plant covers two sites\": the five\n165|  `N-strict-*` rows patch the shared `strictMembers` body used by both frame\n166|  sites (one gate, two call sites); say so.\n167|- **P3-s `native_type` width edge** (`R2-native-type-width-513`, `native.go:118`)\n168|  SURVIVED 2/2 — inside the stated per-edge bound; listed for completeness\n169|  because the bound's text names directives, call IDs and tool names but not\n170|  `native_type`.\n171|- **P3-t LOGBOOK layering.** The leaf's block still opens with rev1 figures\n172|  (25 tests, 49 mutants, pin `69d156d9…`, cases=144) and only the REV2 lines\n173|  carry the shipped state (80 PASS lines, 65 rows, pin `4bd01143…`, 145);\n174|  acceptable as history, but the REV2 line repeats the P1-b sentence and\n175|  must be corrected with it.\n176|\n177|## What is clean (verified, not read)\n178|\n179|1. **Invariant 1** (unknown → opaque, almost-known, unknown member, raw refs\n180|   resolve, stable twice): rows 1–5 reproduce; `N-unknown-kind`,\n181|   `N-unknown-kind-wholly`, `N-unknown-member` KILLED 2/2; PB4 (empty\n182|   unknown-class member) seals a zero-length whole-member `opaque_event`;\n183|   PB8 (unknown type with a non-object body) stays opaque, body never read.\n184|2. **Invariant 2** at the claimed members: rows 6–10 reproduce; the\n185|   forbidden-member sweeps hold; `N-protection-encrypted/-signed`,\n186|   `N-foreign-instruction`, `N-foreign-payload-authority`, `N-usage-target`\n187|   KILLED 2/2; `R3-reasons-unsorted` KILLED 2/2 (order pinned).\n188|3. **Invariant 3**: the five-row matrix plus `TestNormalizeResultAfterBoundaryCompletes`,\n189|   `TestNormalizeProtectedToolCallStaysOpaqueHistory`,\n190|   `TestNormalizeLiveSurfaceStaysEmpty` reproduce; live surface empty in\n191|   every row; `N-tool-incomplete`, `N-tool-orphan`, `N-callable`,\n192|   `N-callable-false`, `N-live-followup`, `N-result-status-pending` KILLED 2/2.\n193|4. **Invariant 4**: main-null parent, contiguous ordinals, predecessor\n194|   parents, single head; 65536 inline / 65537 blob-referenced and byte-exact;\n195|   `N-overflow-bound`, `N-overflow-truncate`, `N-main-parent`,\n196|   `N-parents-chain` KILLED 2/2; PB3 version literals and PB9 (escaped-key\n197|   duplicate) refuse; PB5 (CRLF) keeps the CR inside the byte range.\n198|5. **Determinism / durability**: `TestNormalizeIsDeterministic`,\n199|   `TestNormalizeActorOrderIsDeterministic`, idempotent shared-sink replay and\n200|   no-partial-bundle reproduce; `N-actors-sort` KILLED 2/2.\n201|6. **Story-close**: edited registry is the adopted `ownership.v0.7.0.json`;\n202|   the diff is additive plus the two binding upgrades (trunk's mesh-RPC cases\n203|   intact; the only deleted lines are the two superseded `unevidenced`\n204|   bindings and figure rewrites); digest re-derived = pin; `tracecheck`,\n205|   `--section 7.8`, `--section 10.2` green with the quoted lines byte-equal;\n206|   `traceability` and `cmd/tracecheck` suites PASS including\n207|   `TestREADMEMeasuredCoverageMatchesTracecheckReport` and\n208|   `TestV070RegistryRederivesFromTrunkV060Registry`\n209|   (`logs/pkg-traceability-v.log`); README fenced line byte-equal, prose\n210|   figures consistent with the report; `13.14.1` deliberately unbound with\n211|   the reason stated; 13.14.2–13.14.5 non-ownership stated in matrix D.\n212|7. **Hygiene**: CR paths ⊆ {LOGBOOK, README, clonebundle, cloneproject,\n213|   clonesnap, traceability}; `task-board.config.json` byte-identical to trunk\n214|   (30 commands); the 8 trunk-moved paths that intersect the CR carry only\n215|   additive/figure edits (no reverts); LOGBOOK purely additive and\n216|   newest-first; zero `__pycache__`/`.pyc`; gofmt 0 files, `go build`,\n217|   `go vet`, linux and windows builds, `cataloggen -adopted -check` exit 0.\n218|8. **Suite**: `go test ./... -count=1` 40/41 ok in the copy, the 41st\n219|   (`specpin`) failing only because the copy lacked the tracked\n220|   `.task-board`; re-run with it materialized → ok (`logs/cmd04-*.log`).\n221|   `-race` on cloneproject, clonebundle, clonesnap, traceability/... ok, no\n222|   DATA RACE (`logs/cmd05-race-story-packages.log`); cloneproject coverage\n223|   90.1%. The other 37 packages' race lanes, the fuzz gates and\n224|   `task-board validate` are accepted from the CR construction log\n225|   (`required=30 green=30 failed=0`) and the producer's `cmds/cmd05a-g`\n226|   (41 ok, 0 DATA RACE) — not re-run by me.\n227|\n228|## Coverage ratio I measured\n229|\n230|38 of 38 matrix rows are driven through `Normalize` by a named committed\n231|test over `clonesnap.Capture` output (all 80 PASS lines re-run). Measured\n232|clean at the class level: 34 of 38 — rows 5 (never guessed / re-typed), 8\n233|(never promoted), 9 (foreign instruction low-authority) and 16 (attribution)\n234|hold for the witnessed vectors and fail on the case-alias axis (P1-b).\n235|Outside the matrix, one of the ten emitted kinds (`reasoning_summary`) has\n236|no positive row (P2-d). Reviewer plants: 8 rows against the whole suite,\n237|2/2 each — R1 KILLED (by message), R3 KILLED, R2/R4/R5/R6/R7 SURVIVED,\n238|`RC-control-comment` SURVIVED (`mutants/reviewer-run{1,2}-battery.log`).\n239|Producer battery: 64 KILLED + 1 control SURVIVED, 2/2.\n240|\n241|## Rework scope (for the producer)\n242|\n243|1. P1-b: read the six claimed envelope members from the strict map (no\n244|   second decoder; the 12-line shape in `logs/fixprobe-strict-map-envelope.log`\n245|   is proven green), add one committed row per AC-relevant alias axis\n246|   (kind, origin/authority, protection/promotion, body/content, evidence\n247|   identity, actor) plus a narrowing that restores the case-folded read for\n248|   exactly one member, and correct the five prose sites (`native.go`,\n249|   TRACEABILITY :34/:65/:96, README, LOGBOOK REV2, results).\n250|2. P2-d: one positive `reasoning_summary` row (kind, `internal`, content,\n251|   `exact`) with the routing swap as its narrowing.\n252|3. P3-m..t: capture-status assertions per kind; pin or drop last-wins; pin\n253|   the external actor kind; unknown-type-without-body row; state or refuse\n254|   `text:null`; relabel `N-pending-aborted` and the shared-site `N-strict-*`\n255|   rows; fix the LOGBOOK REV2 sentence.\n256|4. Re-run the battery twice on the final tree, re-run tracecheck, report the\n257|   measured ratio; keep the candidate UNCOMMITTED.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
