{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c69d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b42c-6247-7d31-b9d8-d87c5b1f64f4"},"sequence":425,"recorded_at":1780531400000845,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"0dc60d48-0449-4263-a4d2-db59edd40fb4","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"0dc60d48-0449-4263-a4d2-db59edd40fb4","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"0dc60d48-0449-4263-a4d2-db59edd40fb4"},"call_id":"call_01a0b42dca6d7545ab5531e14be2b452","text":"Read text file `internal/cloneproject/dispatch.go`.\n1|package cloneproject\n2|\n3|// This file dispatches projection units to Canonical Event kinds,\n4|// builds every event and the session through the landed builders,\n5|// and re-decodes each sealed byte before it enters the result.\n6|\n7|import (\n8|\t\"encoding/json\"\n9|\t\"sort\"\n10|\t\"strings\"\n11|\n12|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/clonebundle\"\n13|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n14|)\n15|\n16|// isReasoningType reports whether the native type is a reasoning\n17|// type. Protected reasoning becomes opaque_reasoning; protected\n18|// anything else becomes opaque_event.\n19|func isReasoningType(nativeType string) bool {\n20|\tswitch nativeType {\n21|\tcase nativeReasoningSummary, nativeReasoningCrypt, nativeReasoningSigned:\n22|\t\treturn true\n23|\tdefault:\n24|\t\treturn false\n25|\t}\n26|}\n27|\n28|// dispatchUnits selects kind, visibility, payload, and reasons for\n29|// every unit. Protection is decided before type: unreadable content\n30|// never reaches a semantic kind.\n31|func (plan *projectionPlan) dispatchUnits() error {\n32|\tresolutions := map[string]ToolResolution{}\n33|\tfor _, resolution := range plan.resolutions {\n34|\t\tresolutions[resolution.CallID] = resolution\n35|\t}\n36|\tfor index := range plan.units {\n37|\t\tunit := &plan.units[index]\n38|\t\tif unit.memberOpaque {\n39|\t\t\tunit.kind = \"opaque_event\"\n40|\t\t\tunit.visibility = \"opaque\"\n41|\t\t\tunit.payload = map[string]any{\n42|\t\t\t\t\"native_item_key\":    unit.record.MemberKey,\n43|\t\t\t\t\"byte_count\":         unit.record.Length,\n44|\t\t\t\t\"blob_descriptor_id\": unit.descriptorID,\n45|\t\t\t\t\"extensions\":         map[string]any{},\n46|\t\t\t}\n47|\t\t\tunit.reasons = []string{reasonUnknownNative}\n48|\t\t\tcontinue\n49|\t\t}\n50|\t\tif err := plan.dispatchRecord(unit, resolutions); err != nil {\n51|\t\t\treturn err\n52|\t\t}\n53|\t}\n54|\treturn nil\n55|}\n56|\n57|// dispatchRecord dispatches one parsed record.\n58|func (plan *projectionPlan) dispatchRecord(unit *projectionUnit, resolutions map[string]ToolResolution) error {\n59|\trecord := unit.record\n60|\tif record.Protection != \"none\" {\n61|\t\treturn plan.dispatchProtected(unit)\n62|\t}\n63|\tswitch record.NativeType {\n64|\tcase nativeMessageUser, nativeMessageAssistant:\n65|\t\treturn plan.dispatchMessage(unit)\n66|\tcase nativeReasoningSummary:\n67|\t\treturn plan.dispatchMessage(unit)\n68|\tcase nativeReasoningCrypt, nativeReasoningSigned:\n69|\t\twhere := \"record \" + record.MemberKey + \" line \" + itoa(record.Line)\n70|\t\treturn invalid(\"%s declares %s with no protection\", where, record.NativeType)\n71|\tcase nativeInstruction:\n72|\t\treturn plan.dispatchInstruction(unit)\n73|\tcase nativeToolDefinition:\n74|\t\treturn plan.dispatchDefinition(unit)\n75|\tcase nativeToolCall:\n76|\t\treturn plan.dispatchCall(unit, resolutions)\n77|\tcase nativeToolResult:\n78|\t\treturn plan.dispatchResult(unit, resolutions)\n79|\tcase nativeUsage:\n80|\t\treturn plan.dispatchUsage(unit)\n81|\tdefault:\n82|\t\tunit.kind = \"opaque_event\"\n83|\t\tunit.visibility = \"opaque\"\n84|\t\tunit.payload = map[string]any{\n85|\t\t\t\"native_type\":        record.NativeType,\n86|\t\t\t\"byte_count\":         record.Length,\n87|\t\t\t\"blob_descriptor_id\": unit.descriptorID,\n88|\t\t\t\"extensions\":         map[string]any{},\n89|\t\t}\n90|\t\tunit.reasons = []string{reasonUnknownNative}\n91|\t\treturn nil\n92|\t}\n93|}\n94|\n95|// dispatchProtected dispatches a protected record: protection\n96|// defines the body shape (exactly ciphertext, never interpreted),\n97|// and the kind is opaque. Reasoning stays opaque_reasoning;\n98|// anything else becomes opaque_event.\n99|func (plan *projectionPlan) dispatchProtected(unit *projectionUnit) error {\n100|\trecord := unit.record\n101|\twhere := \"record \" + record.MemberKey + \" line \" + itoa(record.Line)\n102|\tif _, err := decodeProtectedBody(record); err != nil {\n103|\t\treturn err\n104|\t}\n105|\tswitch record.NativeType {\n106|\tcase nativeReasoningCrypt:\n107|\t\tif record.Protection != \"encrypted\" {\n108|\t\t\treturn invalid(\"%s declares reasoning/encrypted with protection %q\", where, record.Protection)\n109|\t\t}\n110|\tcase nativeReasoningSigned:\n111|\t\tif record.Protection != \"signed\" {\n112|\t\t\treturn invalid(\"%s declares reasoning/signed with protection %q\", where, record.Protection)\n113|\t\t}\n114|\t}\n115|\treasons := cryptoReasons(record)\n116|\tif !knownNativeType(record.NativeType) {\n117|\t\treasons = append(reasons, reasonUnknownNative)\n118|\t\tsort.Strings(reasons)\n119|\t}\n120|\tif isReasoningType(record.NativeType) {\n121|\t\tunit.kind = \"opaque_reasoning\"\n122|\t\tunit.visibility = \"opaque\"\n123|\t\tunit.payload = map[string]any{\n124|\t\t\t\"protection\":         record.Protection,\n125|\t\t\t\"byte_count\":         record.Length,\n126|\t\t\t\"blob_descriptor_id\": unit.descriptorID,\n127|\t\t\t\"extensions\":         map[string]any{},\n128|\t\t}\n129|\t\tunit.reasons = reasons\n130|\t\treturn nil\n131|\t}\n132|\tunit.kind = \"opaque_event\"\n133|\tunit.visibility = \"opaque\"\n134|\tunit.payload = map[string]any{\n135|\t\t\"native_type\":        record.NativeType,\n136|\t\t\"protection\":         record.Protection,\n137|\t\t\"byte_count\":         record.Length,\n138|\t\t\"blob_descriptor_id\": unit.descriptorID,\n139|\t\t\"extensions\":         map[string]any{},\n140|\t}\n141|\tunit.reasons = reasons\n142|\treturn nil\n143|}\n144|\n145|// cryptoReasons selects the stable reason for a protected record:\n146|// the foreign core reason when the origin is foreign, no reason\n147|// when native (no core code fits native-protected content; the\n148|// payload protection fact carries the cause).\n149|func cryptoReasons(record NativeRecord) []string {\n150|\tif record.Origin != \"foreign\" {\n151|\t\treturn nil\n152|\t}\n153|\tif record.Protection == \"signed\" {\n154|\t\treturn []string{reasonForeignSigned}\n155|\t}\n156|\treturn []string{reasonForeignEncrypted}\n157|}\n158|\n159|// dispatchMessage dispatches a message or reasoning summary: the\n160|// exact text body becomes one text content block, inline or\n161|// overflow-referenced.\n162|func (plan *projectionPlan) dispatchMessage(unit *projectionUnit) error {\n163|\trecord := unit.record\n164|\tbody, err := decodeMessageBody(record)\n165|\tif err != nil {\n166|\t\treturn err\n167|\t}\n168|\tblock, installed, err := contentBlockForText(body.Text, plan.request.CanonicalSink)\n169|\tif err != nil {\n170|\t\treturn err\n171|\t}\n172|\tplan.overflows = append(plan.overflows, installed...)\n173|\tswitch record.NativeType {\n174|\tcase nativeMessageUser:\n175|\t\tunit.kind = \"user_message\"\n176|\t\tunit.visibility = \"public\"\n177|\tcase nativeMessageAssistant:\n178|\t\tunit.kind = \"assistant_message\"\n179|\t\tunit.visibility = \"public\"\n180|\tdefault:\n181|\t\tunit.kind = \"reasoning_summary\"\n182|\t\tunit.visibility = \"internal\"\n183|\t}\n184|\tunit.payload = map[string]any{\n185|\t\t\"content_blocks\": []any{block},\n186|\t\t\"extensions\":     map[string]any{},\n187|\t}\n188|\treturn nil\n189|}\n190|\n191|// dispatchInstruction dispatches an instruction snapshot: foreign\n192|// instructions pin low authority, native instructions carry their\n193|// claimed authority.\n194|func (plan *projectionPlan) dispatchInstruction(unit *projectionUnit) error {\n195|\trecord := unit.record\n196|\tbody := unit.instruction\n197|\tauthority := body.Authority\n198|\tif record.Origin != \"native\" {\n199|\t\tauthority = \"low\"\n200|\t}\n201|\tdirectives := make([]any, 0, len(body.Directives))\n202|\tfor _, directive := range body.Directives {\n203|\t\tdirectives = append(directives, directive)\n204|\t}\n205|\tunit.kind = \"instruction_snapshot\"\n206|\tunit.visibility = \"internal\"\n207|\tunit.payload = map[string]any{\n208|\t\t\"authority\":  authority,\n209|\t\t\"directives\": directives,\n210|\t\t\"extensions\": map[string]any{},\n211|\t}\n212|\treturn nil\n213|}\n214|\n215|// dispatchDefinition dispatches a tool definition snapshot: history\n216|// with callable pinned false. Registration never happens here; the\n217|// live surface refused live claims before dispatch ran.\n218|func (plan *projectionPlan) dispatchDefinition(unit *projectionUnit) error {\n219|\tbody := unit.definition\n220|\tunit.kind = \"tool_definition_snapshot\"\n221|\tunit.visibility = \"internal\"\n222|\tunit.payload = map[string]any{\n223|\t\t\"tool_name\":         body.ToolName,\n224|\t\t\"definition_digest\": body.DefinitionHash,\n225|\t\t\"callable\":          false,\n226|\t\t\"extensions\":        map[string]any{},\n227|\t}\n228|\treturn nil\n229|}\n230|\n231|// dispatchCall dispatches a tool call with its folded resolution.\n232|func (plan *projectionPlan) dispatchCall(unit *projectionUnit, resolutions map[string]ToolResolution) error {\n233|\tbody := unit.call\n234|\tresolution, ok := resolutions[body.CallID]\n235|\tif !ok {\n236|\t\treturn invalid(\"tool call %q has no folded resolution\", body.CallID)\n237|\t}\n238|\tunit.kind = \"tool_call\"\n239|\tunit.visibility = \"internal\"\n240|\tunit.payload = map[string]any{\n241|\t\t\"call_id\":    body.CallID,\n242|\t\t\"tool_name\":  body.ToolName,\n243|\t\t\"resolution\": resolution.Status,\n244|\t\t\"extensions\": map[string]any{},\n245|\t}\n246|\tif resolution.Status == StatusAborted {\n247|\t\tunit.reasons = []string{reasonUnsafePending}\n248|\t}\n249|\treturn nil\n250|}\n251|\n252|// dispatchResult dispatches a tool result with its folded\n253|// resolution: completed when paired, aborted history when orphaned.\n254|func (plan *projectionPlan) dispatchResult(unit *projectionUnit, resolutions map[string]ToolResolution) error {\n255|\tbody := unit.result\n256|\tresolution, ok := resolutions[body.CallID]\n257|\tif !ok {\n258|\t\treturn invalid(\"tool result %q has no folded resolution\", body.CallID)\n259|\t}\n260|\tunit.kind = \"tool_result\"\n261|\tunit.visibility = \"internal\"\n262|\tunit.payload = map[string]any{\n263|\t\t\"call_id\":    body.CallID,\n264|\t\t\"status\":     body.Status,\n265|\t\t\"resolution\": resolution.Status,\n266|\t\t\"extensions\": map[string]any{},\n267|\t}\n268|\tif resolution.Status == StatusAborted {\n269|\t\tunit.reasons = []string{reasonUnsafePending}\n270|\t}\n271|\treturn nil\n272|}\n273|\n274|// dispatchUsage dispatches a usage report: source tokens into the\n275|// payload; target accounting is never written anywhere.\n276|func (plan *projectionPlan) dispatchUsage(unit *projectionUnit) error {\n277|\tbody := unit.usage\n278|\tunit.kind = \"usage\"\n279|\tunit.visibility = \"internal\"\n280|\tunit.payload = map[string]any{\n281|\t\t\"input_tokens\":  body.InputTokens,\n282|\t\t\"output_tokens\": body.OutputTokens,\n283|\t\t\"extensions\":    map[string]any{},\n284|\t}\n285|\treturn nil\n286|}\n287|\n288|// actorSet is the resolved actor UUIDs by selector.\n289|type actorSet struct {\n290|\tmain  scalar.UUIDv7\n291|\textra map[string]scalar.UUIDv7\n292|}\n293|\n294|// checkActors resolves every referenced selector: main plus exactly\n295|// the mapped extras. A referenced selector without a mapping, or a\n296|// mapping without a reference, refuses.\n297|func (plan *projectionPlan) checkActors() error {\n298|\treferenced := map[string]bool{}\n299|\tfor _, unit := range plan.units {\n300|\t\treferenced[unit.record.Actor] = true\n301|\t}\n302|\tfor selector := range referenced {\n303|\t\tif selector == \"main\" {\n304|\t\t\tcontinue\n305|\t\t}\n306|\t\tif _, ok := plan.extraActors[selector]; !ok {\n307|\t\t\treturn invalid(\"projection references actor %q with no mapped UUID\", selector)\n308|\t\t}\n309|\t}\n310|\tfor selector := range plan.extraActors {\n311|\t\tif !referenced[selector] {\n312|\t\t\treturn invalid(\"projection maps actor %q with no referencing record\", selector)\n313|\t\t}\n314|\t}\n315|\treturn nil\n316|}\n317|\n318|// buildEvents dispatches every unit and seals the events in record\n319|// order: contiguous ordinals from zero, each event parented on its\n320|// predecessor, each sealed byte re-decoded before use.\n321|func (plan *projectionPlan) buildEvents() error {\n322|\tif err := plan.dispatchUnits(); err != nil {\n323|\t\treturn err\n324|\t}\n325|\tactors := actorSet{main: plan.mainActor, extra: plan.extraActors}\n326|\tvar previous *scalar.Digest\n327|\tfor index := range plan.units {\n328|\t\tunit := &plan.units[index]\n329|\t\tactor, ok := actors.extra[unit.record.Actor]\n330|\t\tif unit.record.Actor == \"main\" {\n331|\t\t\tactor, ok = actors.main, true\n332|\t\t}\n333|\t\tif !ok {\n334|\t\t\treturn invalid(\"projection cannot resolve actor %q to a mapped UUID\", unit.record.Actor)\n335|\t\t}\n336|\t\tparents := []string{}\n337|\t\tif previous != nil {\n338|\t\t\tparents = []string{previous.String()}\n339|\t\t}\n340|\t\tpayload, err := json.Marshal(unit.payload)\n341|\t\tif err != nil {\n342|\t\t\treturn invalid(\"projection cannot marshal event payload: %v\", err)\n343|\t\t}\n344|\t\tinput := clonebundle.CanonicalEventInput{\n345|\t\t\tLogicalSessionID: plan.logical.String(),\n346|\t\t\tOrdinal:          uint64(index),\n347|\t\t\tParents:          parents,\n348|\t\t\tActorID:          actor.String(),\n349|\t\t\tKind:             unit.kind,\n350|\t\t\tVisibility:       unit.visibility,\n351|\t\t\tPayload:          payload,\n352|\t\t\tEvidence:         plan.evidenceFor(unit),\n353|\t\t\tExtensions:       map[string]any{},\n354|\t\t}\n355|\t\tsealed, err := clonebundle.BuildCanonicalEvent(input)\n356|\t\tif err != nil {\n357|\t\t\treturn invalid(\"projection cannot seal ordinal %d (%s): %v\", index, unit.kind, err)\n358|\t\t}\n359|\t\tdecoded, err := clonebundle.DecodeCanonicalEvent(sealed)\n360|\t\tif err != nil {\n361|\t\t\treturn invalid(\"sealed ordinal %d refused: %v\", index, err)\n362|\t\t}\n363|\t\tplan.events = append(plan.events, sealed)\n364|\t\tplan.decodedEvents = append(plan.decodedEvents, decoded)\n365|\t\tplan.ordinals = append(plan.ordinals, uint64(index))\n366|\t\tidentifier := decoded.EventID\n367|\t\tprevious = &identifier\n368|\t}\n369|\tif err := clonebundle.CheckOrdinalContiguity(plan.ordinals); err != nil {\n370|\t\treturn err\n371|\t}\n372|\treturn nil\n373|}\n374|\n375|// evidenceFor builds the Source Evidence input for one unit: exact\n376|// capture status with the record's byte range inside its member\n377|// blob, so every reference resolves back to captured bytes.\n378|func (plan *projectionPlan) evidenceFor(unit *projectionUnit) clonebundle.EvidenceInput {\n379|\trecord := unit.record\n380|\tinput := clonebundle.EvidenceInput{\n381|\t\tEnvironment:     plan.environment,\n382|\t\tNativeSessionID: plan.raw.SourceNativeSessionID,\n383|\t\tRawRefs: []clonebundle.RawRefInput{{\n384|\t\t\tManifestID:       plan.raw.ManifestID.String(),\n385|\t\t\tBlobDescriptorID: unit.descriptorID,\n386|\t\t\tOffset:           record.Offset,\n387|\t\t\tLength:           record.Length,\n388|\t\t}},\n389|\t\tCaptureStatus: \"exact\",\n390|\t\tReasonCodes:   append([]string(nil), unit.reasons...),\n391|\t}\n392|\tif !unit.memberOpaque {\n393|\t\teventID := record.NativeEventID\n394|\t\tnativeType := record.NativeType\n395|\t\tinput.NativeEventID = &eventID\n396|\t\tinput.NativeType = &nativeType\n397|\t}\n398|\treturn input\n399|}\n400|\n401|// buildResult seals the Canonical Session over the projected\n402|// events: main plus exactly the referenced extras (parented on\n403|// main), ordinal-ordered event IDs, the last event as head.\n404|func (plan *projectionPlan) buildResult() (*NormalizeResult, error) {\n405|\tmain := plan.mainActor.String()\n406|\tinputs := []clonebundle.ActorInput{{\n407|\t\tActorID: main,\n408|\t\tKind:    \"main\",\n409|\t}}\n410|\tselectors := make([]string, 0, len(plan.extraActors))\n411|\tfor selector := range plan.extraActors {\n412|\t\tselectors = append(selectors, selector)\n413|\t}\n414|\tsort.Strings(selectors)\n415|\tfor _, selector := range selectors {\n416|\t\tname := selector\n417|\t\tkind := \"external\"\n418|\t\tif strings.HasPrefix(selector, \"subagent:\") {\n419|\t\t\tkind = \"subagent\"\n420|\t\t}\n421|\t\tparent := main\n422|\t\tinputs = append(inputs, clonebundle.ActorInput{\n423|\t\t\tActorID:        plan.extraActors[selector].String(),\n424|\t\t\tKind:           kind,\n425|\t\t\tParentActorID:  &parent,\n426|\t\t\tName:           &name,\n427|\t\t\tSourceNativeID: &name,\n428|\t\t})\n429|\t}\n430|\teventIDs := make([]string, 0, len(plan.decodedEvents))\n431|\tfor _, decoded := range plan.decodedEvents {\n432|\t\teventIDs = append(eventIDs, decoded.EventID.String())\n433|\t}\n434|\t// Unreachable: Normalize refused the empty projection before\n435|\t// dispatch ran. The guard keeps a headless build a builder\n436|\t// refusal instead of an index panic.\n437|\theads := []string{}\n438|\tif len(eventIDs) > 0 {\n439|\t\theads = []string{eventIDs[len(eventIDs)-1]}\n440|\t}\n441|\tsession, err := clonebundle.BuildCanonicalSession(clonebundle.CanonicalSessionInput{\n442|\t\tLogicalSessionID:      plan.logical.String(),\n443|\t\tSourceEnvironment:     plan.environment,\n444|\t\tSourceNativeSessionID: plan.raw.SourceNativeSessionID,\n445|\t\tTitle:                 plan.request.Title,\n446|\t\tWorkspace:             plan.request.Workspace,\n447|\t\tActors:                inputs,\n448|\t\tEventIDs:              eventIDs,\n449|\t\tHeadEventIDs:          heads,\n450|\t\tExtensions:            map[string]any{},\n451|\t})\n452|\tif err != nil {\n453|\t\treturn nil, invalid(\"projection cannot seal its session: %v\", err)\n454|\t}\n455|\tdecoded, err := clonebundle.DecodeCanonicalSession(session)\n456|\tif err != nil {\n457|\t\treturn nil, invalid(\"sealed session refused: %v\", err)\n458|\t}\n459|\treturn &NormalizeResult{\n460|\t\tSession:         session,\n461|\t\tDecodedSession:  decoded,\n462|\t\tEvents:          plan.events,\n463|\t\tDecodedEvents:   plan.decodedEvents,\n464|\t\tToolResolutions: plan.resolutions,\n465|\t\tLive:            plan.surface,\n466|\t\tInstruction:     plan.instruction,\n467|\t\tUsage:           plan.usage,\n468|\t\tOverflows:       plan.overflows,\n469|\t}, nil\n470|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c69f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b42c-6247-7d31-b9d8-d87c5b1f64f4"},"sequence":426,"recorded_at":1780531400000847,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"0dc60d48-0449-4263-a4d2-db59edd40fb4","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"0dc60d48-0449-4263-a4d2-db59edd40fb4","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"0dc60d48-0449-4263-a4d2-db59edd40fb4"},"call_id":"call_01a0b42dcc0074a19cb1a54e09146eae","text":"Read text file `internal/cloneproject/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n1|# Projection Fidelity Clause Coverage (TASK-260830-32ypr2)\n2|\n3|Owner: `internal/cloneproject`. Authority:\n4|`internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`, Sections 7.8, 10.2, 13.14.1\n5|(the pinned sections are byte-identical to v0.6.0).\n6|This is the FINAL leaf's clause record for the projection-fidelity\n7|closure; the `internal/traceability` registry bindings and re-pin\n8|ship in this leaf as well (see the Story-close section below).\n9|\n10|## Why this package normalizes instead of clonebundle or clonesnap\n11|\n12|The first leaf (`internal/clonebundle`) owns the capture contracts:\n13|the closed manifest/boundary/session/event shapes, their builders\n14|and decoders. The second leaf (`internal/clonesnap`) owns the\n15|capture OPERATION over a real provider store. This package owns\n16|NORMALIZATION: deriving Canonical Sessions and Canonical Events\n17|from captured bytes. Every event and the session seal through the\n18|landed `clonebundle` builders (`BuildCanonicalEvent`,\n19|`BuildCanonicalSession`, `CheckOrdinalContiguity`,\n20|`RefuseUnstableForTarget`, `InstallRawBlob`) and re-decode through\n21|the landed decoders before return; overflow Blob Descriptors seal\n22|through `clonesnap.BuildBlobDescriptor`; no second manifest,\n23|session, event, blob, or identity model exists here.\n24|\n25|## Landed-owner reuse\n26|\n27|| Scope | Owner | Use |\n28||---|---|---|\n29|| Session/event/evidence shapes | `internal/clonebundle` | all Build/Decode/Check/Refuse entries above |\n30|| Overflow descriptor shape | `internal/clonesnap` | `BuildBlobDescriptor` (errors wrapped with the overflow cause) |\n31|| Blob install (no-replace, fsync, verify) | `internal/clonebundle` + `internal/localstore` | `InstallRawBlob`, `ObjectStore.PutBlob` |\n32|| Digests, UUIDv7, timestamps | `internal/scalar` | `ParseDigest`, `SHA256Digest`, `ParseUUIDv7` |\n33|| Character string measure | `internal/environ` | `StringLength` at every native bound |\n34|| Strict JSON framing | `internal/environ` | `DecodeStrictObject` at `strictMembers`: both frame sites (record envelope, per-kind bodies) refuse lone-surrogate escapes, duplicate members, and trailing data before any member is read |\n35|| uint53 value gate | `internal/environ` | `CheckUint53Bounds` at `bodyUint53` and the envelope version check: fractions, exponents, strings, and out-of-range magnitudes refuse as not-a-uint53 |\n36|| Canonical bytes | `internal/canonicaljson` | `Canonicalize`, `CalculateObjectIdentity` (tests resolve overflow descriptors) |\n37|\n38|## Fixture-native per-kind payload fact registry\n39|\n40|Section 13.14.1 requires payloads to carry only their registered\n41|typed facts. The envelope and value model are landed (`checkPayload`\n42|in `clonebundle`); this package registers the exact facts it emits\n43|for each kind it projects. No other Canonical kind is emitted here.\n44|\n45|| Kind | Exact facts |\n46||---|---|\n47|| `user_message`, `assistant_message`, `reasoning_summary` | `content_blocks` (one `text` block, inline at or under 64 KiB, else `blob_descriptor_id` + `media_type`), `extensions` |\n48|| `opaque_reasoning` | `protection` (`encrypted`\\|`signed`), `byte_count`, `blob_descriptor_id`, `extensions` |\n49|| `opaque_event` (unknown record) | `native_type`, `byte_count`, `blob_descriptor_id`, `extensions` |\n50|| `opaque_event` (protected known record) | `native_type`, `protection`, `byte_count`, `blob_descriptor_id`, `extensions` |\n51|| `opaque_event` (unknown member) | `native_item_key`, `byte_count`, `blob_descriptor_id`, `extensions` |\n52|| `instruction_snapshot` | `authority` (`low` forced for foreign), `directives`, `extensions` |\n53|| `tool_definition_snapshot` | `tool_name`, `definition_digest`, `callable` (always false), `extensions` |\n54|| `tool_call` | `call_id`, `tool_name`, `resolution` (`completed`\\|`aborted`), `extensions` |\n55|| `tool_result` | `call_id`, `status` (`ok`\\|`error`), `resolution`, `extensions` |\n56|| `usage` | `input_tokens`, `output_tokens`, `extensions` |\n57|\n58|## Clause map\n59|\n60|| Pinned clause | Production entry | Test |\n61||---|---|---|\n62|| 13.14.1 unknown native records become raw-addressable opaque events | `Normalize`, `dispatchRecord` | `TestNormalizeUnknownRecordBecomesOpaqueEvent` (kind, `opaque` visibility, `unknown_native_event` reason, raw range resolves to the exact line) |\n63|| 13.14.1 almost-known records are never coerced into a neighbouring kind | `dispatchRecord` (exact type switch) | `TestNormalizeAlmostKnownRecordBecomesOpaqueEvent` (`message/smoke` stays `opaque_event`, never `user_message`) |\n64|| 13.14.1 unknown-class members become whole-member opaque events | `collectMembers` | `TestNormalizeUnknownMemberBecomesWholeMemberOpaque` (offset 0, full length, null native IDs, resolves to the whole member) |\n65|| 13.14.1 opaque events are never dropped, guessed, or re-typed | `Normalize` (deterministic order) | `TestNormalizeOpaqueIsStableAcrossProjections` (project twice, byte-identical, still `opaque_event`) |\n66|| 13.14.1 foreign encrypted reasoning is opaque-preserved | `dispatchProtected` | `TestNormalizeForeignEncryptedReasoningStaysOpaque` (`opaque_reasoning`, `foreign_encrypted_payload`, no content members, byte-exact round trip) |\n67|| 13.14.1 foreign signed reasoning is opaque-preserved | `dispatchProtected` | `TestNormalizeForeignSignedReasoningStaysOpaque` (`foreign_signature_unverifiable`, byte-exact) |\n68|| 13.14.1 native protected reasoning stays opaque with no foreign code | `dispatchProtected`, `cryptoReasons` | `TestNormalizeNativeProtectedReasoningStaysOpaque` (empty reasons) |\n69|| 13.14.1 protected known content never reaches a semantic kind | `dispatchProtected` | `TestNormalizeProtectedMessageBecomesOpaqueEvent` (encrypted assistant message is `opaque_event`) |\n70|| 13.14.1 unknown+protected records carry both stable reasons | `dispatchProtected` | `TestNormalizeUnknownProtectedRecordCarriesBothReasons` |\n71|| 13.14.1 foreign instructions are low-authority history | `dispatchInstruction`, `foldInstructions` | `TestNormalizeForeignInstructionCannotChangeEffectiveSnapshot` (effective snapshot native-only, foreign payload pins `low`), `TestNormalizeForeignOnlyInstructionLeavesSnapshotEmpty` |\n72|| 13.14.1 source usage is not target accounting | `foldUsage` | `TestNormalizeSourceUsageIsNotTargetAccounting` (source sums exact, target zero) |\n73|| 13.14.1 historical tools are inert; call+result resolves completed | `resolveToolCalls`, `deriveLiveSurface` | `TestNormalizeToolMatrix/call_with_result` (kinds, `internal` visibility, `completed`, empty live surface) |\n74|| 13.14.1 incomplete calls become aborted history and block pending action | `resolveToolCalls`, `deriveLiveSurface` | `TestNormalizeToolMatrix/call_without_result` (`aborted`, `unsafe_pending_action`, empty live surface), `TestNormalizeToolMatrix/result_without_call` (orphan `aborted`) |\n75|| 13.14.1 results arriving after the boundary complete the same call | `resolveToolCalls` over two captures | `TestNormalizeResultAfterBoundaryCompletes` (first capture `aborted`, second `completed`) |\n76|| 13.14.1 nested calls attribute to a parented subagent actor | `checkActors`, `buildResult` | `TestNormalizeToolMatrix/nested_subagent_call` (subagent actor, parent is main) |\n77|| 13.14.1 definitions never register a callable tool | `deriveLiveSurface`, `dispatchDefinition` | `TestNormalizeToolDefinitionNeverRegistersCallable` (`callable` false, `CallableTools` empty) |\n78|| 13.14.1 live surface stays empty over mixed history | `deriveLiveSurface` | `TestNormalizeLiveSurfaceStaysEmpty` |\n79|| 13.14.1 Canonical Session bounds (actors, ordered event IDs, head) | `buildResult` | `TestNormalizeSealsSessionShape` (ordinals, parent chain, head is last) |\n80|| 13.14.1 message-like inline content at most 64 KiB; oversized becomes a blob reference | `contentBlockForText`, `installOverflow` | `TestNormalizeInlineContentBoundary` (65536 inline, 65537 blob-referenced and byte-exact, never truncated) |\n81|| 13.14.1 same captured bytes project byte-identical output | `Normalize` (sorted inputs, no clock), `buildResult` actor sort | `TestNormalizeIsDeterministic`, `TestNormalizeActorOrderIsDeterministic` (three extra actors, twelve projections, one distinct session) |\n82|| 13.14.1 unstable_archive cannot enter target projection | `Normalize` via `RefuseUnstableForTarget` | `TestNormalizeRefusesUnstableCapture` |\n83|| 13.14.1 capture closure: manifest link, blob fetch, digest/size agreement | `Normalize`, `collectMembers` | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/manifest_closure_drift/tampered_blob/missing_blob/blob_size_drift` (each arm asserts its own message) |\n84|| 13.14.1 framing-malformed records refuse with member+line named | `strictMembers`, `splitRecordLines`, `parseNativeLine`, body decoders | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/malformed_json_line/missing_envelope_member/bad_envelope_version/string_envelope_version/blank_line/unknown_body_member/contradictory_protection/protected_plaintext_body/unknown_protected_plaintext_body/lone_surrogate_text/lone_surrogate_envelope/duplicate_envelope_member/duplicate_body_member/trailing_bytes/invalid_utf8_line` |\n85|| 13.14.1 live claims by captured history refuse | `deriveLiveSurface`, `resolveToolCalls` | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/live_attestation_claim/live_followup_claim` |\n86|| 13.14.1 ambiguous tool pairings refuse | `resolveToolCalls` | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/duplicate_call_id/duplicate_result_id` |\n87|| 13.14.1 exact actor mapping (referenced iff mapped) | `checkActors` | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/unmapped_actor/unmapped_extra_actor/main_actor_in_map` |\n88|| 13.14.1 instruction authority, usage value model, and result status vocabulary | `decodeInstructionBody`, `bodyUint53`, `decodeToolResultBody` | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/bad_instruction_authority/fractional_usage/unsafe_usage_magnitude/string_usage_number/bad_result_status` |\n89|| 13.14.1 reasoning type/protection agreement refuses per arm | `dispatchProtected` | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/encrypted_type_signed_protection/signed_type_encrypted_protection` |\n90|| 13.14.1 protected non-reasoning tool records reach opaque only via the fold-skip | `foldTools` skip, `dispatchProtected` | `TestNormalizeProtectedToolCallStaysOpaqueHistory` (protected call is `opaque_event`, the unprotected result an aborted orphan, live surface empty) |\n91|| 13.14.1 non-JSONL included members refuse the whole projection | `collectMembers` JSONL parsing | `TestNormalizeNonJSONLIncludedMemberRefuses` (stated bound: routing by member class is sibling scope) |\n92|| 10.2 Blob Descriptor reference resolves to installed bytes | `installOverflow` | `TestNormalizeInlineContentBoundary` (`mustResolveOverflow` through the sink) |\n93|| 10.2 fsync + verify + atomic install before referencing | `InstallRawBlob`, `PutBlob` (landed) | `TestNormalizeIsIdempotentIntoSharedSink` (replay verifies and reuses, blob count stable) |\n94|| 7.8 large data by reference, never embedded in the 8 MiB frame | `sessadapter.DecodeRequestFrame` (`MaxFrameBytes`) | `TestDecodeRequestFrameRefusesOversizeFrame`, `TestFrameBoundEdges` (sessadapter owner; `session-adapter-frame-bound` case). `TestNormalizeInlineContentBoundary` proves reference-not-embedded at the content level but constructs no frame and discharges no 7.8 clause |\n95|| 1.6 string measure in characters | `environ.StringLength` at every native bound | `TestNormalizeMultibyteStringMeasure` (512-char ID admits, 513 refuses) and `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/long_subagent_name`; per-edge directive/call/tool-name rows are stated bounds |\n96|| 1.6 text is valid UTF-8, never rewritten | `environ.DecodeStrictObject` at `strictMembers` (both frame sites) after line-level `utf8.Valid` | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/lone_surrogate_text/lone_surrogate_envelope/duplicate_envelope_member/duplicate_body_member/trailing_bytes/invalid_utf8_line` |\n97|\n98|## Durability\n99|\n100|This package holds no local state. Its only durable write is\n101|overflow-blob installation: payload bytes through the landed\n102|`InstallRawBlob` (descriptor identity plus blob-ID/size agreement)\n103|and descriptor bytes through `ObjectStore.PutBlob`, both\n104|content-addressed under the landed no-replace discipline (stage,\n105|fsync, verify, atomic install). Crash semantics are the landed\n106|`localstore` discipline's (proven by that package's fault suites);\n107|this package adds bundle atomicity at the return:\n108|`TestNormalizeFailureReturnsNoPartialBundle` proves a mid-projection\n109|fetch failure returns no partial bundle and a healthy re-run\n110|converges, and `TestNormalizeIsIdempotentIntoSharedSink` proves a\n111|replay into a shared sink seals byte-identical output while the sink\n112|blob count stays stable (verify-and-reuse, no reinstall). A refused\n113|projection may leave orphan overflow blobs from earlier units in the\n114|sink; they are content-addressed and inert, and no bundle ever\n115|references them.\n116|\n117|## Mutants\n118|\n119|`testdata/mutant_harness.py` ships 62 narrowing rows, 2 labelled\n120|non-narrowing rows, and the harmless `C-doc-comment` SURVIVED\n121|control. Every narrowing weakens one gate to admit exactly one\n122|member of the class it must reject, and every killer drives the\n123|production `Normalize` entry over real captured bytes.\n124|`N-native-type-token` and `N-protection-encrypted` are the\n125|token-preserving attacks: the searched-for text still matches\n126|while the decision changes, and the killers execute the\n127|behavioral suite. `N-empty-projection` is labelled single-member\n128|class and `N-overflow-truncate` is labelled behaviour swap; no\n129|other row is an arm-delete, and no plant covers two sites. The\n130|battery runs twice with one raw log per plant per run carrying\n131|the subprocess exit.\n132|\n133|## Stated bounds (sibling scope, not waived)\n134|\n135|- The fixture-native record envelope is test-defined framing, not a\n136|  specification shape: `v`, `native_event_id`, `native_type`,\n137|  `origin`, `protection`, `actor`, `body`. Real providers define\n138|  their own native logs; the adapter layer is `sessadapter` scope.\n139|- Per-kind payload facts cover exactly the registry above. Other\n140|  Canonical kinds (`session_started`, `approval_request`,\n141|  `plan_update`, `progress`, `rate_limit`, `file_change`,\n142|  `compaction`, `turn_*`, `subagent_*`, `error`,\n143|  `migration_checkpoint`, `session_finished`) are never emitted\n144|  here; their fact registries are normalization-sibling scope.\n145|- Framing-malformed lines refuse (unparseable JSON, lone\n146|  surrogate escapes, duplicate members, trailing data, missing\n147|  envelope members, blank lines, invalid UTF-8, contradictory\n148|  protection claims, unknown body members inside a known type)\n149|  instead of projecting: without attributable identity a line\n150|  cannot become evidence. Type-level unknowns become\n151|  `opaque_event`.\n152|- Every included non-unknown member is parsed as the JSONL record\n153|  log: a non-JSONL included member refuses the whole projection\n154|  with member+line named (pinned by\n155|  `TestNormalizeNonJSONLIncludedMemberRefuses`); routing by member\n156|  class is sibling scope.\n157|- Per-edge character-width rows past the envelope ID edge\n158|  (directive 4096/4097, call ID 512/513, tool names) are stated\n159|  bounds: every edge checks through the landed\n160|  `environ.StringLength` gate, but only the envelope ID edge\n161|  carries a narrowing (`N-string-bound`).\n162|- `\"directives\":null` decodes as zero directives: null is not\n163|  distinguished from an empty array at the instruction body.\n164|- Native-protected records carry no reason code: the closed core\n165|  reasons name foreign causes only, and extension reasons are\n166|  operator scope. The payload `protection` fact carries the cause.\n167|- Turn IDs and source timestamps are always null: turns are not\n168|  reconstructed and source clocks are not trusted.\n169|- Tool call arguments are not carried: calls are inert history\n170|  identified by call ID and tool name.\n171|- Unknown-class excluded members project nothing: their bytes were\n172|  never captured.\n173|- Sections 13.14.2-13.14.5 (fidelity dispositions, projection\n174|  planning, Migration Checkpoint, lineage, transaction, tuple\n175|  admission) are sibling scope: this story plans no projection,\n176|  stages no target, and admits no tuple.\n177|- Section 7.8 operation wiring (capture-plan/capture/normalize\n178|  frames) stays owned by `sessadapter`; this package owns the\n179|  fidelity rules those operations must satisfy, not the frames.\n180|- The `pending` live-work-order map parameter of\n181|  `deriveLiveSurface` is live-sibling API: `Normalize` always\n182|  passes nil, so nothing captured can pend.\n183|\n184|## Story-close (FINAL leaf)\n185|\n186|This leaf binds the story's normative sections in\n187|`internal/traceability/ownership.v0.7.0.json`:\n188|\n189|- `section:7.8` is bound FULL (2/2) with a `sessadapter`\n190|  production owner: clause `7.8#1` (large data by reference,\n191|  never embedded in the 8 MiB frame) discharges through the new\n192|  `session-adapter-frame-bound` case\n193|  (`TestDecodeRequestFrameRefusesOversizeFrame` and\n194|  `TestFrameBoundEdges`, both committed by the sessadapter\n195|  owner); clause `7.8#2` (execution bindings equal freshly read\n196|  facts) discharges through the new\n197|  `session-adapter-call-binding` case (`TestCheckCallBinding`\n198|  plus the zero-facts refusal test, both committed by the\n199|  sessadapter owner). The projection overflow reference test\n200|  constructs no adapter frame, so it discharges no 7.8 clause.\n201|- `section:10.2` is bound FULL (5/5): `10.2#1` through\n202|  `clone-capture-contracts`, `10.2#3`–`10.2#5` through\n203|  `clone-native-capture`, and `10.2#2` through\n204|  `clone-native-capture` (capture install),\n205|  `clone-projection-fidelity` (overflow install and idempotent\n206|  replay), and the landed `localstore-immutable-blob-install`\n207|  (the fsync/verify/atomic-install owner). The binding owns the\n208|  union of the eight landed trunk cases and the three clone\n209|  cases.\n210|- `section:13.14.1` carries no RFC 2119 keyword line the\n211|  `tracecheck` scanner can see (its obligations are closed-shape\n212|  \"contains exactly\" sentences), so no registry binding can\n213|  enumerate it: it would measure `unmeasured`, which assigned-scope\n214|  admission deliberately refuses. The story's 13.14.1 clause record\n215|  is therefore the three package `TRACEABILITY.md` files plus the\n216|  three leaf conformance matrices, executed by the three real\n217|  suites bound as `clone-capture-contracts`, `clone-native-capture`,\n218|  and `clone-projection-fidelity`.\n219|- `reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256` in\n220|  `internal/traceability/traceability.go` is re-derived from the\n221|  edited registry (derivation command and output in\n222|  `TASK-260830-32ypr2_results.md`).","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
