{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c779","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b42c-6247-7d31-b9d8-d87c5b1f64f4"},"sequence":535,"recorded_at":1780531400001065,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"0dc60d48-0449-4263-a4d2-db59edd40fb4","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"0dc60d48-0449-4263-a4d2-db59edd40fb4","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"0dc60d48-0449-4263-a4d2-db59edd40fb4"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b42e-0c97-7e92-ba67-1f38f0cb4344"},"task_id":"01a0b42e-0c97-7e92-ba67-1f38f0cb4344","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b42e-0c97-7e92-ba67-1f38f0cb4344","chunk":"Read text file `internal/cloneproject/testdata/mutant_harness.py`.\n1|#!/usr/bin/env python3\n2|\"\"\"Narrowing-mutant harness for internal/cloneproject.\n3|\n4|Every gate ships a narrowing mutant: the gate stays present and is\n5|weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and\n6|the named killer test must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that\n7|the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence.\n8|\n9|Each row runs M (mutate one production file in place), R (run the\n10|scoped Go killer through the production Normalize entry over real\n11|captured bytes), V (verdict from the Go exit code plus a FAIL\n12|kill-line: KILLED iff R fails with a test failure line, SURVIVED iff\n13|R passes, ERROR for anything else — unapplied patches, build breaks,\n14|timeouts). M failures and R infrastructure errors are ERROR, never\n15|kills or survivals. The file is restored from its backup after every\n16|row, pass or fail.\n17|\n18|Rows N-native-type-token and N-protection-encrypted are the\n19|token-preserving attacks: the searched-for text still matches, but\n20|the decision changes. Their killers execute the behavioral Normalize\n21|suite over captured bytes, not a static checker.\n22|\n23|Two rows carry explicit non-narrowing labels instead of the narrowing\n24|claim: N-empty-projection (single-member class: the gate's reject\n25|class holds only the empty projection, so the plant admits the whole\n26|class) and N-overflow-truncate (behaviour swap: truncate to 64 KiB\n27|instead of installing a blob reference).\n28|\n29|Row C-doc-comment is the harmless control: a comment-only edit that\n30|must SURVIVE, proving the harness observes test outcomes instead of\n31|hard-coding kills.\n32|\n33|Usage:\n34|  PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/cloneproject/testdata/mutant_harness.py [--log-dir DIR] [MUTANT ...]\n35|\"\"\"\n36|\n37|import shutil\n38|import subprocess\n39|import sys\n40|import tempfile\n41|import time\n42|from dataclasses import dataclass\n43|from pathlib import Path\n44|\n45|REPO = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[3]\n46|PACKAGE = \"internal/cloneproject\"\n47|\n48|\n49|@dataclass(frozen=True)\n50|class Mutant:\n51|    name: str\n52|    path: str\n53|    find: str\n54|    replace: str\n55|    count: int\n56|    run: str\n57|    expect: str\n58|    note: str\n59|\n60|\n61|MUTANTS = [\n62|    Mutant(\n63|        name=\"N-unknown-kind\",\n64|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/dispatch.go\",\n65|        find='''\\tdefault:\\n\\t\\tunit.kind = \"opaque_event\"\\n''',\n66|        replace='''\\tdefault:\\n\\t\\tunit.kind = \"opaque_event\"\\n\\t\\tif record.NativeType == \"message/smoke\" {\\n\\t\\t\\tunit.kind = \"user_message\"\\n\\t\\t}\\n''',\n67|        count=1,\n68|        run=\"TestNormalizeAlmostKnownRecordBecomesOpaqueEvent\",\n69|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n70|        note=\"Admits exactly message/smoke past the unknown-type gate into user_message; every other unknown type still projects opaque_event.\",\n71|    ),\n72|    Mutant(\n73|        name=\"N-native-type-token\",\n74|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/dispatch.go\",\n75|        find='''\\tcase nativeMessageUser:\\n\\t\\tunit.kind = \"user_message\"\\n''',\n76|        replace='''\\tcase nativeMessageUser:\\n\\t\\tunit.kind = \"assistant_message\"\\n''',\n77|        count=1,\n78|        run=\"TestNormalizeSealsSessionShape\",\n79|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n80|        note=\"Token-preserving: the message/user label still matches but routes to assistant_message; the behavioral killer pins the kind.\",\n81|    ),\n82|    Mutant(\n83|        name=\"N-unknown-member\",\n84|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/normalize.go\",\n85|        find='''\\t\\tif item.Class == \"unknown\" {\\n''',\n86|        replace='''\\t\\tif item.Class == \"unknown\" && item.NativeItemKey != \"store/mystery\" {\\n''',\n87|        count=1,\n88|        run=\"TestNormalizeUnknownMemberBecomesWholeMemberOpaque\",\n89|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n90|        note=\"Admits exactly store/mystery past the unknown-class gate into JSONL parsing; every other unknown member still projects whole-member opaque.\",\n91|    ),\n92|    Mutant(\n93|        name=\"N-protection-encrypted\",\n94|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/dispatch.go\",\n95|        find='''\\tif record.Protection != \"none\" {\\n''',\n96|        replace='''\\tif record.Protection != \"none\" && record.Protection != \"encrypted\" {\\n''',\n97|        count=1,\n98|        run=\"TestNormalizeForeignEncryptedReasoningStaysOpaque\",\n99|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n100|        note=\"Token-preserving narrowing: admits exactly encrypted records past the protection gate; signed records still project opaque.\",\n101|    ),\n102|    Mutant(\n103|        name=\"N-reasoning-contradiction\",\n104|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/dispatch.go\",\n105|        find='''\\tcase nativeReasoningCrypt, nativeReasoningSigned:\\n\\t\\twhere := \"record \" + record.MemberKey + \" line \" + itoa(record.Line)\\n\\t\\treturn invalid(\"%s declares %s with no protection\", where, record.NativeType)\\n''',\n106|        replace='''\\tcase nativeReasoningCrypt, nativeReasoningSigned:\\n\\t\\twhere := \"record \" + record.MemberKey + \" line \" + itoa(record.Line)\\n\\t\\tif record.NativeType == \"reasoning/signed\" {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn invalid(\"%s declares %s with no protection\", where, record.NativeType)\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tunit.kind = \"reasoning_summary\"\\n\\t\\tunit.visibility = \"internal\"\\n\\t\\tunit.payload = map[string]any{\"content_blocks\": []any{}, \"extensions\": map[string]any{}}\\n\\t\\treturn nil\\n''',\n107|        count=1,\n108|        run=\"TestNormalizeRefusalTable/contradictory_protection\",\n109|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n110|        note=\"Admits exactly unprotected reasoning/encrypted as reasoning_summary; unprotected reasoning/signed still refuses.\",\n111|    ),\n112|    Mutant(\n113|        name=\"N-foreign-instruction\",\n114|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/tools.go\",\n115|        find='''\\t\\tif observation.record.Origin != \"native\" {\\n''',\n116|        replace='''\\t\\tif observation.record.Origin != \"native\" && observation.record.NativeEventID != \"evt-inst-foreign\" {\\n''',\n117|        count=1,\n118|        run=\"TestNormalizeForeignInstructionCannotChangeEffectiveSnapshot\",\n119|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n120|        note=\"Admits exactly the foreign instruction into the effective snapshot; every other foreign record stays history-only.\",\n121|    ),\n122|    Mutant(\n123|        name=\"N-foreign-payload-authority\",\n124|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/dispatch.go\",\n125|        find='''\\tauthority := body.Authority\\n\\tif record.Origin != \"native\" {\\n\\t\\tauthority = \"low\"\\n\\t}\\n''',\n126|        replace='''\\tauthority := body.Authority\\n\\tif record.Origin != \"native\" && record.NativeEventID != \"evt-inst-foreign\" {\\n\\t\\tauthority = \"low\"\\n\\t}\\n''',\n127|        count=1,\n128|        run=\"TestNormalizeForeignInstructionCannotChangeEffectiveSnapshot\",\n129|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n130|        note=\"Admits exactly the foreign high claim into the payload authority; every other foreign instruction still pins low.\",\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
