g | Change | Test that fails without it | Evidence path |\n24||---|---|---|---|\n25|| P1-a strict-decode fork: envelope/body decoded with plain `encoding/json`, rewriting lone surrogates and guessing duplicate members last-wins while stamping `exact` | `parseNativeLine` and `decodeBodyObject` decode through the new `strictMembers` helper, which delegates to `environ.DecodeStrictObject` and refuses with the fault named (`is not a JSON object` for syntax faults, `is not a strict JSON object` otherwise); the later struct read is exact because the rewriting/guessing shapes never pass the gate (comment says so); envelope version reads through `environ.CheckUint53Bounds(members[\"v\"], 1, 1)` | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/lone_surrogate_text`, `/lone_surrogate_envelope`, `/duplicate_envelope_member`, `/duplicate_body_member` (new refusal rows asserting the literal `lone surrogate escape` / `duplicate member` faults) | `pkg-cloneproject-v.log`; `mutants/run1/N-strict-*.log` + `run2` (4 narrowings, each admitting exactly its killer fixture into a lenient decode) |\n26|| P2-c `bodyUint53` fork admitting `\"5\"` | `bodyUint53` delegates to `environ.CheckUint53Bounds(raw, 0, maxUint53)`; doc comment fixed (now true: fraction, exponent, sign, magnitude, string all refuse); per-member failures merge into one `is not a uint53` refusal while the ledger sum keeps `exceeds uint53` (message merge documented in the test) | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/string_usage_number` (new), `/string_envelope_version` (new); `/fractional_usage` and `/unsafe_usage_magnitude` keep refusing through the delegation | `mutants/run1/N-usage-string.log`, `N-usage-number.log`, `N-usage-magnitude.log`, `N-envelope-version.log`, `N-envelope-version-string.log` (+ `run2`) |\n27|| P2-a inherited advisories dropped + false prose | One decision line per group below; `clonesnap/project.go` comment and `clonesnap/TRACEABILITY.md` bullets rewritten to state what the tree does (pinning tests named, deferral owners name