xes: the base proof\n62|plus the 3-actor/12-projection proof; row 23 extended to the 45-row\n63|refusal table); rows 25–38 are new:\n64|\n65|- Strict framing (25–28): lone-surrogate text/envelope members and\n66|  duplicate envelope/body members refuse with the fault named —\n67|  never rewritten, never coerced, never guessed.\n68|- Value model (29): string-typed numbers refuse at the usage body\n69|  and the envelope version.\n70|- Determinism (30), agreement arms (31), protected-tool fold-skip\n71|  (32), result-status vocabulary (33), size arm (34), trailing\n72|  bytes (35), unknown+protected body decision (36).\n73|- Pinned bounds (37–38): non-JSONL included members refuse;\n74|  null directives decode as empty.\n75|\n76|Measured, not planned: every gate row carries a directly-reddening\n77|narrowing (62 narrowings + 2 labelled rows, battery green twice).\n78|Disclosed non-narrowed members: row 15 post-boundary (gate-level\n79|only — the same `resolveToolCalls` decision row 13 narrows);\n80|rows 18/19/21 shape internals (owned by the accepted clonebundle\n81|suite, stated per member); row 24 (failure-injection proofs, no\n82|gate); row 37 (enforcing gate narrowed by the strict-decode rows);\n83|row 38 (admitted shape, no gate). No row is prose-only.\n84|\n85|## Mutants\n86|\n87|`internal/cloneproject/testdata/mutant_harness.py`: 62 narrowing\n88|rows + 2 labelled non-narrowing rows (`N-empty-projection`\n89|single-member class, `N-overflow-truncate` behaviour swap) +\n90|harmless `C-doc-comment` SURVIVED control. Battery executed TWICE\n91|on the final tree, exit 0 both runs, 65/65 `ok:` lines each, one\n92|raw log per plant per run carrying the mutant identity, patch,\n93|subprocess exit, and FAIL line (`mutants/run1/`, `mutants/run2/`,\n94|`run1-battery.log`, `run2-battery.log` in the archive).\n95|Token-preserving rows: `N-native-type-token` and\n96|`N-protection-encrypted` — both killers execute the behavioral\n97|`Normalize` suite over captured bytes. No plant covers two sites.\n98|`PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, zero `__pycache__`/`.pyc` (verified\n99|after the runs). Cross-check: the six re-anchorable rev1 reviewer\n100|plant shapes (R1 actors-unsorted, R2 encrypted-admits-signed,\n101|R5 protected-tools-folded, R6 status-pending, R7 size-skipped,\n102|R8 unknown-protected-skipped) were applied by hand to the final\n103|tree and all KILLED firsthand by the new tests; R3/R3b are the\n104|stated P3-c bound and R4's anchor is deleted by the delegation\n105|(covered by `N-trailing-admitted`).\n106|\n107|## Story-close (rev2 deltas)\n108|\n109|- Registry: new `session-adapter-frame-bound` case (production\n110|  `internal/sessadapter/protocol.go` `DecodeRequestFrame`, tests\n111|  `TestDecodeRequestFrameRefusesOversizeFrame` +\n112|  `TestFrameBoundEdges`); `section:7.8` production moved to\n113|  `sessadapter`, cases `[session-adapter-frame-bound,\n114|  session-adapter-call-binding]`, `7.8#1` discharges through the\n115|  frame case; `section:10.2` owns the 11-case union and `10.2#2`\n116|  gains `localstore-immutable-blob-install`. Trunk's mesh-RPC\n117|  cases and upgraded bindings intact (additive + the two reviewed\n118|  binding upgrades).\n119|- Pin re-derivation (gate-computed, never copied):\n120|\n121|  ```\n122|  $ go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck\n123|  spec-to-code traceability check failed: ownership registry projection digest 4bd01143702d17bc05f187a14312cb868b85276b0f0b6d015c351929eae9bfc0 differs from reviewed 69d156d99a3b13ae598c7de3152225eafe4576c8f33286e8e36f68f22235052a\n124|  exit status 1\n125|  ```\n126|\n127|  Pinned `4bd01143702d17bc05f187a14312cb868b85276b0f0b6d015c351929eae9bfc0`\n128|  in `traceability.go`. The gate reached the digest check with no\n129|  earlier failure, structurally validating the edited registry.\n130|- `tracecheck` green, quoted verbatim:\n131|\n132|  ```\n133|  traceability ok: contracts=64 normative_sections=36 acceptance_cases=145 fixtures=33 compatibility_contracts=55 assigned_scopes=0\n134|  section coverage: bindings=68 full=4 partial=8 sliver=5 unevidenced=47 unmeasured=4 unowned=7 clauses_discharged=63/569\n135|  ```\n136|\n137|  Section runs (both admitted, `assigned_scopes=1`, same coverage\n138|  line): `--section 7.8` exit 0, `--section 10.2` exit 0 (logs\n139|  `section-7.8.log`, `section-10.2.log`).\n140|- `section:13.14.1` deliberately unbound (no scanner-visible RFC\n141|  2119 line; a binding would measure `unmeasured` and fail\n142|  assigned scope).\n143|- Pin tests: report wants 145; rederivation gate carries the\n144|  literal 7.8/10.2 upgrades + the five literal clone/sessadapter\n145|  cases; `main_test.go` wants lines carry 145 (both arms).\n146|- README: 145 ownership figure; 7.8 at 2/2 bound to\n147|  `internal/sessadapter` (frame-bound case + call-binding case);\n148|  Nine sessadapter cases; clone-story admissions list gains the\n149|  frame case and `localstore-immutable-blob-install`; 10.2 prose\n150|  notes the union; fenced coverage line byte-equal (figures\n151|  unchanged: 63/569, four full, forty-seven unevidenced).\n152|- LOGBOOK: REV2 block appended to the leaf entry (newest-first\n153|  preserved).\n154|- `task-board.config.json` byte-identical to trunk (no validation\n155|  command added; verified with `cmp` after the run — see below).\n156|\n157|## Validation reran (this run, final tree — nothing accepted from prior runs)\n158|\n159|All 30 configured commands, exits observed firsthand (logs\n160|`cmds/cmd01.log` … `cmds/cmd30.log` in the archive; race gate as\n161|`cmd05a` … `cmd05g`):\n162|\n163|- 1 gofmt check: 0. 2 build: 0. 3 vet: 0.\n164|- 4 `go test ./... -count=1 -v`: 0 — 41 packages `ok`, 2499\n165|  top-level PASS, zero FAIL.\n166|- 5 race gate: 0 in 7 bounded groups (7+6+6+6+6+9+1 = 41\n167|  packages `ok`, zero `DATA RACE`, zero FAIL; `sessquery` alone\n168|  in group G at 309s), each with `-timeout 25m`, instead of one\n169|  long call per the headless time bound.\n170|-