{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c865","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b42c-6247-7d31-b9d8-d87c5b1f64f4"},"sequence":653,"recorded_at":1780531400001301,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"0dc60d48-0449-4263-a4d2-db59edd40fb4","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"0dc60d48-0449-4263-a4d2-db59edd40fb4","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"0dc60d48-0449-4263-a4d2-db59edd40fb4"},"call_id":"call_01a0b42e4648778fa5a4e05cbeab8893","text":"Read text file `.temp/TASK-260830-32ypr2/rev2-review/res/TASK-260830-32ypr2_conformance-matrix.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-32ypr2 Conformance Matrix (rev2) — test-unknown-encrypted-and-incomplete-events\n2|\n3|Authority: `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`, Sections 7.8, 10.2, 13.14.1.\n4|Production entry for every row: `Normalize` (`internal/cloneproject/normalize.go:97`).\n5|Every proof builds an on-disk fixture provider store, runs the real\n6|`clonesnap.Capture` entry (`internal/clonesnap/capture.go`), then `Normalize`\n7|over the sealed manifests and installed blobs. No row drives hand-written\n8|Canonical Events or calls an unexported helper directly (verified: no test\n9|references `dispatchRecord`, `dispatchProtected`, `resolveToolCalls`,\n10|`deriveLiveSurface`, `foldInstructions`, `foldUsage`, `contentBlockForText`,\n11|`installOverflow`, `parseNativeLine`, `collectMembers`, `splitRecordLines`,\n12|`strictMembers`, `bodyUint53`, `decodeBodyObject`, `bodyString`, or\n13|`checkActorSelector`).\n14|\n15|## A. AC coverage: 38 of 38 rows driven and measured\n16|\n17|One row per behavior the brief's four invariants name plus the\n18|rework-mandated strict-framing, value-model, and gate rows. \"Narrowing\"\n19|names the harness row(s) in\n20|`internal/cloneproject/testdata/mutant_harness.py` that redden the\n21|row's killer(s); every narrowing admits exactly one member of the\n22|class its gate must reject. \"(killer)\" marks the plant whose\n23|committed killer is the row's test; other entries name the shared\n24|gate the plant narrows. Battery: 62 narrowings + 2 labelled rows\n25|KILLED + control SURVIVED, executed twice, exit 0 both runs, one\n26|raw log per plant per run under `mutants/run1/` + `mutants/run2/`\n27|in the producer evidence archive.\n28|\n29|| # | AC behavior | Driving test(s) → call site | Narrowing(s) |\n30||---|---|---|---|\n31|| 1 | Wholly unknown native type → `opaque_event`, `opaque` visibility, `unknown_native_event` reason, identity kept | `TestNormalizeUnknownRecordBecomesOpaqueEvent` → `Normalize` → `dispatchRecord` default arm | `N-unknown-kind-wholly` (killer: admits exactly `frobnicate` into `user_message`) |\n32|| 2 | Almost-known record (right envelope, unknown inner type) never coerced into a neighbouring kind | `TestNormalizeAlmostKnownRecordBecomesOpaqueEvent` → same arm | `N-unknown-kind` (killer: admits exactly `message/smoke` into `user_message`) |\n33|| 3 | Unknown-class member → whole-member `opaque_event` (offset 0, full length, null native IDs) | `TestNormalizeUnknownMemberBecomesWholeMemberOpaque` → `Normalize` → `collectMembers` | `N-unknown-member` (killer: admits exactly `store/mystery` into JSONL parsing) |\n34|| 4 | Evidence ranges resolve to the exact captured bytes (manifest + descriptor linkage, in range) | `mustResolveRef` assertions in rows 1–3 tests + `mustResolveOverflow` in row 20 test; single-ref evidences asserted `len==1` (trivially sorted/unique) | `N-digest-verify`, `N-missing-blob` (fetch-integrity gates, killers on the refusal rows) |\n35|| 5 | Never dropped, guessed, or re-typed on a second projection | `TestNormalizeOpaqueIsStableAcrossProjections` (`Normalize` ×2 over fresh sinks, byte-equal, still `opaque_event`) | gate-level: rows 1–3 narrowings pin the kinds; rows 25–28 pin the no-guess axes (strict framing); structural: `Normalize` holds no cross-call state |\n36|| 6 | Foreign encrypted reasoning → `opaque_reasoning`, `foreign_encrypted_payload`, no content members, byte-exact round trip | `TestNormalizeForeignEncryptedReasoningStaysOpaque` → `Normalize` → `dispatchProtected` | `N-protection-encrypted` (killer; token-preserving: the `encrypted` label still matches, the decision changes) |\n37|| 7 | Foreign signed reasoning → `opaque_reasoning`, `foreign_signature_unverifiable`, byte-exact | `TestNormalizeForeignSignedReasoningStaysOpaque` → same gate | `N-protection-signed` (killer: admits exactly `signed` past the gate) |\n38|| 8 | Never decrypted, re-encoded, summarized, truncated, or promoted; native-protected carries no foreign code; protected known content never semantic; unknown+protected carries both reasons | `TestNormalizeNativeProtectedReasoningStaysOpaque` + `TestNormalizeProtectedMessageBecomesOpaqueEvent` + `TestNormalizeUnknownProtectedRecordCarriesBothReasons` + forbidden-member sweeps (`content_blocks`, `content`, `text`, `ciphertext`, `summary` absent) in rows 6–7 tests | `N-native-reason-foreign` (killer), `N-reasons-both-single` (killer), `N-protection-encrypted` cross-kill on the protected-message test (verified by hand probe at rev1, `crosskill-encrypted-vs-protected-message.log`: exit 1 under the plant, `ok` restored) |\n39|| 9 | Foreign instructions are low-authority history: cannot change the effective snapshot or authority | `TestNormalizeForeignInstructionCannotChangeEffectiveSnapshot` + `TestNormalizeForeignOnlyInstructionLeavesSnapshotEmpty` → `foldInstructions` / `dispatchInstruction` | `N-foreign-instruction`, `N-foreign-payload-authority` (killers) |\n40|| 10 | Source usage never becomes target accounting | `TestNormalizeSourceUsageIsNotTargetAccounting` → `foldUsage` | `N-usage-target` (killer); `N-usage-number`, `N-usage-string`, `N-usage-magnitude`, `N-usage-overflow` (value model) |\n41|| 11 | `tool_definition_snapshot` is history, `callable` false, never registers; live claims refuse | `TestNormalizeToolDefinitionNeverRegistersCallable` + refusal row `live_attestation_claim` → `dispatchDefinition` / `deriveLiveSurface` | `N-callable-false`, `N-callable` (killers) |\n42|| 12 | Call with result → `completed`, `internal` visibility, empty live surface | `TestNormalizeToolMatrix/call_with_result` → `resolveToolCalls` / `dispatchCall` | `N-pending-completed` (killer) |\n43|| 13 | Call without result → `aborted`, `unsafe_pending_action`, blocks pending action | `TestNormalizeToolMatrix/call_without_result` → same | `N-tool-incomplete`, `N-pending-aborted` (killers) |\n44|| 14 | Result without call → `aborted` orphan | `TestNormalizeToolMatrix/result_without_call` → `resolveToolCalls` / `dispatchResult` | `N-tool-orphan` (killer) |\n45|| 15 | Result arriving after the capture boundary completes the same call | `TestNormalizeResultAfterBoundaryCompletes` (first capture `aborted`, second `completed`) → same pairing decision | gate-level: `N-tool-incomplete` (same `resolveToolCalls` decision; no dedicated plant — disclosed) |\n46|| 16 | Nested/subagent call attributes to a parented subagent actor, never main | `TestNormalizeToolMatrix/nested_subagent_call` → `checkActors` / `buildResult` | `N-subagent-actor` (killer) |\n47|| 17 | `internal` visibility and no pending action for every matrix row; live surface empty over mixed history | visibility assertions in every matrix subtest + `TestNormalizeLiveSurfaceStaysEmpty` → `deriveLiveSurface` | `N-pending-aborted`, `N-pending-completed`, `N-live-followup` (killers on the named rows) |\n48|| 18 | Canonical Event exact shape: contiguous ordinals from zero, predecessor parents, UUIDv7 actors, literal kinds/visibilities, landed re-decode of every sealed byte | `TestNormalizeSealsSessionShape` → `buildEvents` → `clonebundle.BuildCanonicalEvent` + `DecodeCanonicalEvent` | `N-parents-chain`, `N-native-type-token` (killers; token-preserving) |\n49|| 19 | Source Evidence `exact` status with stable reason codes | reason assertions in rows 1, 6, 7, 13 tests → `evidenceFor` | `N-reasons-both-single`, `N-native-reason-foreign` (killers) |\n50|| 20 | 64 KiB edge: 65536-byte text inline, 65537-byte text a byte-exact blob reference, never a truncation | `TestNormalizeInlineContentBoundary` → `contentBlockForText` / `installOverflow` | `N-overflow-bound` (killer); `N-overflow-truncate` (labelled behaviour swap, killer) |\n51|| 21 | Canonical Session shape: main + referenced extras, ordinal-ordered unique IDs, last event as head, parent null only for main | `TestNormalizeSealsSessionShape` (incl. `ParentActorID == nil` for main) + row 16 subagent-parent assertion → `buildResult` → `clonebundle.BuildCanonicalSession` + decode | `N-main-parent` (killer: admits exactly main to the parented class; the landed builder refuses), `N-parents-chain` |\n52|| 22 | Determinism: same captured bytes → byte-identical session + events twice, along both axes | `TestNormalizeIsDeterministic` (base proof) + `TestNormalizeActorOrderIsDeterministic` (3 extra actors × 12 projections, one distinct session) | `N-actors-sort` (killer on the actor-order axis: leaves exactly the 3-actor shape unsorted) |\n53|| 23 | Every refusal through `Normalize` naming the member, line, or blob | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable` (45 subtests) + `TestNormalizeRefusesUnstableCapture` + `TestNormalizeRefusesEnvironmentDrift` | one narrowing per family, each killing its row: `N-envelope-version`, `N-envelope-version-string`, `N-origin`, `N-protection-value`, `N-actor-selector`, `N-malformed-json`, `N-blank-line`, `N-body-member`, `N-instruction-authority`, `N-directive-count`, `N-definition-digest`, `N-usage-number`, `N-usage-string`, `N-usage-magnitude`, `N-usage-overflow`, `N-duplicate-call`, `N-duplicate-result`, `N-live-followup`, `N-callable`, `N-actor-unmapped-fallback`, `N-actor-unreferenced`, `N-main-in-map`, `N-subagent-name`, `N-manifest-link`, `N-missing-blob`, `N-digest-verify`, `N-size-verify`, `N-empty-projection` (labelled single-member class), `N-unstable`, `N-env-drift`, `N-string-bound`, `N-reasoning-contradiction`, `N-reasoning-encrypted-signed`, `N-reasoning-signed-encrypted`, `N-result-status-pending`, `N-unknown-protected-body`, `N-strict-text-surrogate`, `N-strict-envelope-surrogate`, `N-strict-envelope-duplicate`, `N-strict-body-duplicate`, `N-trailing-admitted` |\n54|| 24 | No partial bundle on failure; idempotent replay into a shared sink (byte-identical output, stable blob count) | `TestNormalizeFailureReturnsNoPartialBundle` + `TestNormalizeIsIdempotentIntoSharedSink` | none: failure-injection proofs, not gates; crash semantics of the write itself owned by `internal/localstore` (landed fault suites) |\n55|| 25 | Lone-surrogate text member refuses, never rewritten to U+FFFD | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/lone_surrogate_text` → `Normalize` → `strictMembers` + `environ.DecodeStrictObject` (line and body frame sites) | `N-strict-text-surrogate` (killer: admits exactly the killer line past the strict gate at both frame sites into a lenient decode) |\n56|| 26 | Lone-surrogate envelope member refuses, evidence identity never rewritten | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/lone_surrogate_envelope` → same gate | `N-strict-envelope-surrogate` (killer) |\n57|| 27 | Duplicate envelope member refuses, never coerced into a neighbouring kind | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/duplicate_envelope_member` → same gate | `N-strict-envelope-duplicate` (killer: last-wins decode coerces into `user_message` under the plant) |\n58|| 28 | Duplicate body member refuses, never guessed last-wins | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/duplicate_body_member` → same gate | `N-strict-body-duplicate` (killer) |\n59|| 29 | String-typed numbers refuse: a uint53 member is a JSON integer | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/string_usage_number` + `/string_envelope_version` → `bodyUint53` / envelope version check + `environ.CheckUint53Bounds` | `N-usage-string`, `N-envelope-version-string` (killers) |\n60|| 30 | Actor-order determinism over ≥2 extra actors | `TestNormalizeActorOrderIsDeterministic` → `buildResult` actor sort | `N-actors-sort` (killer) |\n61|| 31 | Reasoning type/protection agreement refuses per arm | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/encrypted_type_signed_protection` + `/signed_type_encrypted_protection` → `dispatchProtected` | `N-reasoning-encrypted-signed`, `N-reasoning-signed-encrypted` (killers) |\n62|| 32 | Protected non-reasoning tool records reach opaque only via the fold-skip | `TestNormalizeProtectedToolCallStaysOpaqueHistory` → `foldTools` skip + `dispatchProtected` | `N-protected-tools-skip` (killer: the admitted call refuses on its ciphertext body under the plant) |\n63|| 33 | Result status vocabulary is exactly `ok|error` | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/bad_result_status` → `decodeToolResultBody` | `N-result-status-pending` (killer: the call resolves `completed` under the plant) |\n64|| 34 | Size arm refuses with its own message before the digest arm | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/blob_size_drift` (+ `tampered_blob` asserting `blob digest disagrees`) → `collectMembers` | `N-size-verify` (killer: the drift reaches the digest arm with its different message under the plant) |\n65|| 35 | Trailing bytes refuse | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/trailing_bytes` → `strictMembers` + landed gate | `N-trailing-admitted` (killer: the lenient decode refuses with a different message under the plant) |\n66|| 36 | Unknown+protected non-ciphertext body refuses (decided: only exactly-`ciphertext` protected bodies project opaque) | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/unknown_protected_plaintext_body` → `dispatchProtected` | `N-unknown-protected-body` (killer: projects `opaque_event` under the plant) |\n67|| 37 | Non-JSONL included members refuse the whole projection (stated bound, pinned) | `TestNormalizeNonJSONLIncludedMemberRefuses` (binary index + text cache subtests) → `collectMembers` JSONL parsing | gate-level: the strict-decode narrowings pin the enforcing gate; no dedicated plant (bound — disclosed) |\n68|| 38 | Null directives decode as empty (stated bound, pinned) | `TestNormalizeNullDirectivesDecodeAsEmpty` → `decodeInstructionBody` | none: admitted shape, not a gate (disclosed) |\n69|\n70|Ratio: **38 of 38 AC rows driven** through the production entry by named\n71|committed tests. No row is prose-only.\n72|\n73|## B. Registry bindings claimed by this Story (tracecheck-measured)\n74|\n75|| Clause | Acceptance case → executing test(s) | Measured |\n76||---|---|---|\n77|| `7.8#1` large data by reference, never embedded in the 8 MiB frame | `session-adapter-frame-bound` → `TestDecodeRequestFrameRefusesOversizeFrame`, `TestFrameBoundEdges` (production `internal/sessadapter/protocol.go` `DecodeRequestFrame`, sessadapter owner) | full 2/2, `--section 7.8` admitted |\n78|| `7.8#2` execution bindings equal fresh facts | `session-adapter-call-binding` → `TestCheckCallBinding`, `TestCheckCallBindingZeroFactsRefuse` (sessadapter owner) | full 2/2 |\n79|| `10.2#1` metadata in manifest | `clone-capture-contracts` → `TestBuildRawManifestRoundTrip`, `TestBuildCaptureManifestDerivesRawComplete`, `TestBuildCanonicalEventRoundTrip`, `TestRawManifestRefusals`, `TestCaptureManifestRefusals` | full 5/5, `--section 10.2` admitted |\n80|| `10.2#2` fsync + verify + atomic install | `clone-native-capture` → `TestCaptureSealsBothManifestsFromStoreBytes`, `TestCaptureInstallsEveryPayloadBlob`, `TestCaptureMultiChunkMember`, `TestCaptureLogRecordsDigestsOnly`, `TestCaptureRefusesOversizedMember`; plus `clone-projection-fidelity` → `TestNormalizeIsIdempotentIntoSharedSink`; plus `localstore-immutable-blob-install` (the landed fsync/verify/atomic-install owner) | full 5/5 |\n81|| `10.2#3` digest-only metrics | `clone-native-capture` (same suite) | full 5/5 |\n82|| `10.2#4` chunk agreement | `clone-native-capture` (same suite) | full 5/5 |\n83|| `10.2#5` oversize refuses `capability_unavailable` | `clone-native-capture` (same suite) | full 5/5 |\n84|\n85|The `section:10.2` binding owns the union of the eight landed trunk\n86|cases (`scalar-digest-validation`,\n87|`scalar-bounded-integer-validation`, `canonical-jcs-rfc8785`,\n88|`canonical-object-identity`, `canonical-identity-refusal`,\n89|`localstore-digest-path-v1`, `localstore-immutable-blob-install`,\n90|`localstore-sqlite-projection`) and the three clone cases. The\n91|projection overflow reference test (`TestNormalizeInlineContentBoundary`)\n92|constructs no adapter frame and discharges no 7.8 clause.\n93|\n94|`section:13.14.1` is deliberately NOT BOUND in the registry: the section\n95|carries no RFC 2119 keyword line the `tracecheck` scanner can see (its\n96|obligations are closed-shape \"contains exactly\" sentences), so any binding\n97|would measure `unmeasured`, which assigned-scope admission deliberately\n98|refuses. The Story's 13.14.1 record is the three package `TRACEABILITY.md`\n99|files plus the three leaf matrices, executed by the three real suites bound\n100|above as `clone-capture-contracts`, `clone-native-capture`, and\n101|`clone-projection-fidelity`. This leaf's 13.14.1 rows are section C below.\n102|\n103|## C. Section 13.14.1 clause record (this leaf)\n104|\n105|Each row names the committed test that executes it through `Normalize`;\n106|full entry + note detail lives in `internal/cloneproject/TRACEABILITY.md`\n107|(Clause map), which this matrix incorporates.\n108|\n109|| Pinned clause | Test |\n110||---|---|\n111|| Unknown native records become raw-addressable opaque events | `TestNormalizeUnknownRecordBecomesOpaqueEvent` |\n112|| Almost-known records never coerced into a neighbouring kind | `TestNormalizeAlmostKnownRecordBecomesOpaqueEvent` |\n113|| Unknown-class members become whole-member opaque events | `TestNormalizeUnknownMemberBecomesWholeMemberOpaque` |\n114|| Opaque events never dropped, guessed, or re-typed | `TestNormalizeOpaqueIsStableAcrossProjections` |\n115|| Foreign encrypted reasoning is opaque-preserved | `TestNormalizeForeignEncryptedReasoningStaysOpaque` |\n116|| Foreign signed reasoning is opaque-preserved | `TestNormalizeForeignSignedReasoningStaysOpaque` |\n117|| Native protected reasoning stays opaque with no foreign code | `TestNormalizeNativeProtectedReasoningStaysOpaque` |\n118|| Protected known content never reaches a semantic kind | `TestNormalizeProtectedMessageBecomesOpaqueEvent` |\n119|| Unknown+protected records carry both stable reasons | `TestNormalizeUnknownProtectedRecordCarriesBothReasons` |\n120|| Foreign instructions are low-authority history | `TestNormalizeForeignInstructionCannotChangeEffectiveSnapshot`, `TestNormalizeForeignOnlyInstructionLeavesSnapshotEmpty` |\n121|| Null directives decode as empty (stated bound) | `TestNormalizeNullDirectivesDecodeAsEmpty` |\n122|| Source usage is not target accounting | `TestNormalizeSourceUsageIsNotTargetAccounting` |\n123|| Historical tools inert; call+result resolves completed | `TestNormalizeToolMatrix/call_with_result` |\n124|| Incomplete calls become aborted history and block pending action | `TestNormalizeToolMatrix/call_without_result`, `TestNormalizeToolMatrix/result_without_call` |\n125|| Protected tool calls stay opaque history via the fold-skip | `TestNormalizeProtectedToolCallStaysOpaqueHistory` |\n126|| Results arriving after the boundary complete the same call | `TestNormalizeResultAfterBoundaryCompletes` |\n127|| Nested calls attribute to a parented subagent actor | `TestNormalizeToolMatrix/nested_subagent_call` |\n128|| Definitions never register a callable tool | `TestNormalizeToolDefinitionNeverRegistersCallable` |\n129|| Live surface stays empty over mixed history | `TestNormalizeLiveSurfaceStaysEmpty` |\n130|| Canonical Session bounds (actors, ordered event IDs, head) | `TestNormalizeSealsSessionShape` |\n131|| Inline content at most 64 KiB; oversized becomes a blob reference | `TestNormalizeInlineContentBoundary` |\n132|| Same captured bytes project byte-identical output | `TestNormalizeIsDeterministic`, `TestNormalizeActorOrderIsDeterministic` |\n133|| `unstable_archive` cannot enter target projection | `TestNormalizeRefusesUnstableCapture` |\n134|| Manifest link, blob fetch, digest/size agreement (each arm its own message) | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/manifest_closure_drift`, `/tampered_blob`, `/missing_blob`, `/blob_size_drift` |\n135|| Framing-malformed records refuse with member+line named | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/malformed_json_line`, `/missing_envelope_member`, `/bad_envelope_version`, `/string_envelope_version`, `/blank_line`, `/unknown_body_member`, `/contradictory_protection`, `/protected_plaintext_body`, `/unknown_protected_plaintext_body`, `/lone_surrogate_text`, `/lone_surrogate_envelope`, `/duplicate_envelope_member`, `/duplicate_body_member`, `/trailing_bytes`, `/invalid_utf8_line` |\n136|| Reasoning type/protection agreement refuses per arm | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/encrypted_type_signed_protection`, `/signed_type_encrypted_protection` |\n137|| Live claims by captured history refuse | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/live_attestation_claim`, `/live_followup_claim` |\n138|| Ambiguous tool pairings refuse | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/duplicate_call_id`, `/duplicate_result_id` |\n139|| Exact actor mapping (referenced iff mapped) | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/unmapped_actor`, `/unmapped_extra_actor`, `/main_actor_in_map` |\n140|| Instruction authority, usage value model, and result status vocabulary | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/bad_instruction_authority`, `/fractional_usage`, `/unsafe_usage_magnitude`, `/string_usage_number`, `/bad_result_status` |\n141|| Non-JSONL included members refuse (stated bound) | `TestNormalizeNonJSONLIncludedMemberRefuses` |\n142|| Blob Descriptor reference resolves to installed bytes | `TestNormalizeInlineContentBoundary` (`mustResolveOverflow`) |\n143|| Fsync + verify + atomic install before referencing | `TestNormalizeIsIdempotentIntoSharedSink` |\n144|| Large data by reference at the content level (discharges no 7.8 clause) | `TestNormalizeInlineContentBoundary` |\n145|| String measure in characters | `TestNormalizeMultibyteStringMeasure`, `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/long_subagent_name` (per-edge directive/call/tool-name rows are stated bounds) |\n146|| Text is valid UTF-8, never rewritten | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/lone_surrogate_text`, `/lone_surrogate_envelope`, `/duplicate_envelope_member`, `/duplicate_body_member`, `/trailing_bytes`, `/invalid_utf8_line` (gate: `environ.DecodeStrictObject` at `strictMembers`) |\n147|\n148|## D. Stated bounds and NOT APPLICABLE (with owners)\n149|\n150|| Area | Status | Owner / evidence |\n151||---|---|---|\n152|| Fixture-native record envelope (`v`, `native_event_id`, `native_type`, `origin`, `protection`, `actor`, `body`) | Stated bound: test-defined framing, not a specification shape; body shapes exact, envelope extras unclaimed | this leaf (`doc.go`, `native.go` + refusal rows) |\n153|| Canonical kinds never emitted here (`session_started`, `approval_request`, `plan_update`, `progress`, `rate_limit`, `file_change`, `compaction`, `turn_*`, `subagent_*`, `error`, `migration_checkpoint`, `session_finished`) | NOT APPLICABLE: fact registries cover exactly the ten emitted kinds | normalization-sibling scope |\n154|| Non-text content blocks (`json`, `image`, `audio`, `document`, `resource_link`, `redacted`, `opaque`) | NOT APPLICABLE: this leaf seals `text` blocks only (inline or blob-referenced) | normalization-sibling scope; closed vocabulary enforced by the landed builder |\n155|| Capture statuses `partial`, `synthesized`, `unavailable` | NOT APPLICABLE: this leaf emits `exact` only | shape rules owned by the accepted `internal/clonebundle` suite |\n156|| Closed-shape internals (26-kind registry, 0..64 parents sorted-unique, UUIDv7, turn/time nullability, extensions, session scale bounds 1024/1M/1024) | Shape rules owned by the accepted `internal/clonebundle` suite; this leaf proves its output satisfies them by sealing + re-decoding every event and session (builder refusal = projection error) | `internal/clonebundle` (leaf 1, accepted) |\n157|| Actor UUIDv7 parsing | Gate owned by `internal/scalar`; entry refusal pinned by `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/bad_actor_uuid` | `internal/scalar` (landed) |\n158|| `parent_actor_id` shape rule (null iff main) | Enforced by the landed builder; main-null asserted in `TestNormalizeSealsSessionShape`, subagent-parent in `nested_subagent_call`, wiring narrowed by `N-main-parent` | `internal/clonebundle` builder + this leaf |\n159|| Closed core reason vocabulary (`unknown_native_event`, `foreign_encrypted_payload`, `foreign_signature_unverifiable`, `unsafe_pending_action`, …) | Referenced, not owned: defined by §13.14.2; this leaf emits four codes as evidence strings without implementing dispositions | §13.14.2 owner (sibling) |\n160|| §13.14.2 fidelity dispositions, projection planning, lineage | NOT APPLICABLE: sibling scope | §13.14.2 owner (sibling) |\n161|| §13.14.3 Migration Checkpoint / bundle chain | NOT APPLICABLE: sibling scope | §13.14.3 owner (sibling) |\n162|| §13.14.4 transaction / staging | NOT APPLICABLE: this Story plans no projection, stages no target | §13.14.4 owner (sibling) |\n163|| §13.14.5 tuple admission | NOT APPLICABLE: this Story admits no tuple | §13.14.5 owner (sibling) |\n164|| §7.8 operation frames (capture-plan/capture/normalize) and the 8 MiB frame bound | NOT APPLICABLE here: owned and discharged by `sessadapter` (`session-adapter-frame-bound` case); this leaf owns the fidelity rules those operations must satisfy | `internal/sessadapter` (landed) |\n165|| Per-edge character-width rows past the envelope ID edge (directive 4096/4097, call ID 512/513, tool names) | Stated bound: every edge checks through the landed `environ.StringLength` gate, but only the envelope ID edge carries a narrowing (`N-string-bound`) | this leaf (deferred rows) |\n166|| Non-JSONL included members | Stated bound, pinned: every included non-unknown member parses as the JSONL log; routing by member class is sibling scope | this leaf (`TestNormalizeNonJSONLIncludedMemberRefuses`) |\n167|| `directives:null` | Stated bound, pinned: decodes as zero directives | this leaf (`TestNormalizeNullDirectivesDecodeAsEmpty`) |\n168|| Durable-write crash semantics (stage/fsync/verify/atomic install) | Owned by `internal/localstore` (landed fault suites); this leaf adds bundle atomicity (row 24) | `internal/localstore` (landed) |\n169|| `pending` live-work-order map parameter of `deriveLiveSurface` | Live-sibling API: `Normalize` always passes nil, so nothing captured can pend | live sibling (stated bound) |\n170|| Inherited advisories P3-a, P3-b, P3-c/d, P3-f, P3-g (capture-operation rows) | DEFERRED to a follow-up on `internal/clonesnap` (orchestrator-routed); this leaf changes no clonesnap behavior | clonesnap follow-up |\n171|| Inherited P3-e AfterWalk-seam bound | CLOSED here as a stated bound (`internal/clonesnap/TRACEABILITY.md` + results) | this leaf |\n172|| Inherited P3-η `EncodeNativeIdentity` standalone contract | DEFERRED to a follow-up on the `internal/clonebundle` owner | clonebundle owner follow-up |\n173|| Inherited P3-ζ′ fidelity vocabulary spelled twice | BOUND: both spellings named with pinning tests; unification deferred to a follow-up on `internal/sessadapter` + `internal/clonesnap` | sessadapter/clonesnap follow-up |\n174|| Inherited P3-ζ lone surrogate | CLOSED here at the projection entry (rows 25–26 + narrowings) | this leaf |\n175|| `ax` command, `doctor` result, runtime capability | NOT CLAIMED anywhere in code, tests, README, or LOGBOOK | — |\n176|\n177|## E. Negative-evidence index\n178|\n179|Every refusal below is driven through `Normalize` over real captured bytes\n180|by the named committed test and reddened by the named narrowing (single\n181|member admitted). Production call sites: `Normalize` (`normalize.go`),\n182|`collectMembers` + `sealedEnvironment` (closure), `strictMembers` +\n183|`parseNativeLine` + `splitRecordLines` + body decoders (`native.go`),\n184|`dispatchRecord` / `dispatchProtected` (`dispatch.go`), `resolveToolCalls` +\n185|`deriveLiveSurface` (`tools.go`), `checkActors` + `buildEvents` +\n186|`buildResult` (`dispatch.go`).\n187|\n188|Refusal rows (45 in `TestNormalizeRefusalTable` + 3 standalone:\n189|`TestNormalizeRefusesUnstableCapture`,\n190|`TestNormalizeRefusesEnvironmentDrift`,\n191|`TestNormalizeNonJSONLIncludedMemberRefuses`): see section\n192|A rows 11, 13, 17, 23, 25–29, 31, 33–37 and section C. Token-preserving attacks:\n193|`N-native-type-token` (the `message/user` label still matches, routes to\n194|`assistant_message`; killer `TestNormalizeSealsSessionShape` executes the\n195|behavioral suite) and `N-protection-encrypted` (the `encrypted` label still\n196|matches, skips opaque dispatch; killer `TestNormalizeForeignEncryptedReasoningStaysOpaque`).\n197|Labelled non-narrowings: `N-empty-projection` (single-member class)\n198|and `N-overflow-truncate` (behaviour swap).\n199|Harmless control: `C-doc-comment` (comment-only edit, SURVIVED exit 0 both\n200|runs), proving the harness observes outcomes instead of hard-coding kills.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c867","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b42c-6247-7d31-b9d8-d87c5b1f64f4"},"sequence":654,"recorded_at":1780531400001303,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"0dc60d48-0449-4263-a4d2-db59edd40fb4","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"0dc60d48-0449-4263-a4d2-db59edd40fb4","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"0dc60d48-0449-4263-a4d2-db59edd40fb4"},"call_id":"call_01a0b42e4895742480c1febb7b7bd654","text":"Read text file `internal/cloneproject/tools_test.go`.\n1|package cloneproject\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"testing\"\n5|)\n6|\n7|// Invariant 3: historical tools are inert and incomplete calls never\n8|// become live actions. The matrix drives every pairing shape through\n9|// Normalize over real captured bytes and asserts the projected kind,\n10|// the visibility, the folded resolution, and the empty live surface.\n11|\n12|func TestNormalizeToolMatrix(t *testing.T) {\n13|\tcall := func(id, tool string) string {\n14|\t\treturn rec(\"evt-\"+id, \"tool/call\", \"native\", \"none\", \"main\",\n15|\t\t\t`{\"call_id\":\"`+id+`\",\"tool_name\":\"`+tool+`\"}`)\n16|\t}\n17|\tresult := func(id, status string) string {\n18|\t\treturn rec(\"evt-\"+id+\"-result\", \"tool/result\", \"native\", \"none\", \"main\",\n19|\t\t\t`{\"call_id\":\"`+id+`\",\"status\":\"`+status+`\"}`)\n20|\t}\n21|\tt.Run(\"call_with_result\", func(t *testing.T) {\n22|\t\tbundle := projectMembers(t, []fixtureMember{\n23|\t\t\t{key: \"store/session.jsonl\", class: \"durable_payload\", content: jsonl(\n24|\t\t\t\tcall(\"call-1\", \"read\"),\n25|\t\t\t\tresult(\"call-1\", \"ok\"),\n26|\t\t\t)},\n27|\t\t})\n28|\t\tresolved := bundle.result\n29|\t\tif len(resolved.ToolResolutions) != 1 {\n30|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"len(ToolResolutions) = %d, want 1\", len(resolved.ToolResolutions))\n31|\t\t}\n32|\t\tif resolved.ToolResolutions[0].Status != \"completed\" {\n33|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"Status = %q, want completed\", resolved.ToolResolutions[0].Status)\n34|\t\t}\n35|\t\tcallEvent := eventByNativeID(t, resolved, \"evt-call-1\")\n36|\t\tif callEvent.Kind != \"tool_call\" {\n37|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"Kind = %q, want tool_call\", callEvent.Kind)\n38|\t\t}\n39|\t\tif callEvent.Visibility != \"internal\" {\n40|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"Visibility = %q, want internal\", callEvent.Visibility)\n41|\t\t}\n42|\t\tif payloadText(t, callEvent, \"resolution\") != \"completed\" {\n43|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"payload resolution = %q, want completed\", payloadText(t, callEvent, \"resolution\"))\n44|\t\t}\n45|\t\tif len(callEvent.Evidence.ReasonCodes) != 0 {\n46|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"ReasonCodes = %q, want empty for a completed call\", callEvent.Evidence.ReasonCodes)\n47|\t\t}\n48|\t\tresultEvent := eventByNativeID(t, resolved, \"evt-call-1-result\")\n49|\t\tif resultEvent.Kind != \"tool_result\" {\n50|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"Kind = %q, want tool_result\", resultEvent.Kind)\n51|\t\t}\n52|\t\tif payloadText(t, resultEvent, \"resolution\") != \"completed\" {\n53|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"payload resolution = %q, want completed\", payloadText(t, resultEvent, \"resolution\"))\n54|\t\t}\n55|\t\tif len(resolved.Live.CallableTools) != 0 || len(resolved.Live.PendingActions) != 0 {\n56|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"Live = %+v, want empty\", resolved.Live)\n57|\t\t}\n58|\t})\n59|\tt.Run(\"call_without_result\", func(t *testing.T) {\n60|\t\tbundle := projectMembers(t, []fixtureMember{\n61|\t\t\t{key: \"store/session.jsonl\", class: \"durable_payload\", content: jsonl(\n62|\t\t\t\tcall(\"call-7\", \"write\"),\n63|\t\t\t)},\n64|\t\t})\n65|\t\tresolved := bundle.result\n66|\t\tif len(resolved.ToolResolutions) != 1 {\n67|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"len(ToolResolutions) = %d, want 1\", len(resolved.ToolResolutions))\n68|\t\t}\n69|\t\tif resolved.ToolResolutions[0].Status != \"aborted\" {\n70|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"Status = %q, want aborted\", resolved.ToolResolutions[0].Status)\n71|\t\t}\n72|\t\tcallEvent := eventByNativeID(t, resolved, \"evt-call-7\")\n73|\t\tif callEvent.Kind != \"tool_call\" {\n74|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"Kind = %q, want tool_call\", callEvent.Kind)\n75|\t\t}\n76|\t\tif callEvent.Visibility != \"internal\" {\n77|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"Visibility = %q, want internal\", callEvent.Visibility)\n78|\t\t}\n79|\t\tif payloadText(t, callEvent, \"resolution\") != \"aborted\" {\n80|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"payload resolution = %q, want aborted\", payloadText(t, callEvent, \"resolution\"))\n81|\t\t}\n82|\t\tif len(callEvent.Evidence.ReasonCodes) != 1 || callEvent.Evidence.ReasonCodes[0] != \"unsafe_pending_action\" {\n83|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"ReasonCodes = %q, want [unsafe_pending_action]\", callEvent.Evidence.ReasonCodes)\n84|\t\t}\n85|\t\tif len(resolved.Live.CallableTools) != 0 || len(resolved.Live.PendingActions) != 0 {\n86|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"Live = %+v, want empty\", resolved.Live)\n87|\t\t}\n88|\t})\n89|\tt.Run(\"result_without_call\", func(t *testing.T) {\n90|\t\tbundle := projectMembers(t, []fixtureMember{\n91|\t\t\t{key: \"store/session.jsonl\", class: \"durable_payload\", content: jsonl(\n92|\t\t\t\tresult(\"call-ghost\", \"ok\"),\n93|\t\t\t)},\n94|\t\t})\n95|\t\tresolved := bundle.result\n96|\t\tif len(resolved.ToolResolutions) != 1 {\n97|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"len(ToolResolutions) = %d, want 1\", len(resolved.ToolResolutions))\n98|\t\t}\n99|\t\tif resolved.ToolResolutions[0].Status != \"aborted\" {\n100|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"Status = %q, want aborted\", resolved.ToolResolutions[0].Status)\n101|\t\t}\n102|\t\torphan := eventByNativeID(t, resolved, \"evt-call-ghost-result\")\n103|\t\tif orphan.Kind != \"tool_result\" {\n104|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"Kind = %q, want tool_result\", orphan.Kind)\n105|\t\t}\n106|\t\tif orphan.Visibility != \"internal\" {\n107|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"Visibility = %q, want internal\", orphan.Visibility)\n108|\t\t}\n109|\t\tif payloadText(t, orphan, \"resolution\") != \"aborted\" {\n110|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"payload resolution = %q, want aborted\", payloadText(t, orphan, \"resolution\"))\n111|\t\t}\n112|\t\tif len(orphan.Evidence.ReasonCodes) != 1 || orphan.Evidence.ReasonCodes[0] != \"unsafe_pending_action\" {\n113|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"ReasonCodes = %q, want [unsafe_pending_action]\", orphan.Evidence.ReasonCodes)\n114|\t\t}\n115|\t\tif len(resolved.Live.CallableTools) != 0 || len(resolved.Live.PendingActions) != 0 {\n116|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"Live = %+v, want empty\", resolved.Live)\n117|\t\t}\n118|\t})\n119|\tt.Run(\"nested_subagent_call\", func(t *testing.T) {\n120|\t\tmembers := []fixtureMember{\n121|\t\t\t{key: \"store/session.jsonl\", class: \"durable_payload\", content: jsonl(\n122|\t\t\t\trec(\"evt-nested-call\", \"tool/call\", \"native\", \"none\", \"subagent:fetch\",\n123|\t\t\t\t\t`{\"call_id\":\"call-nested\",\"tool_name\":\"fetch\"}`),\n124|\t\t\t\trec(\"evt-nested-result\", \"tool/result\", \"native\", \"none\", \"subagent:fetch\",\n125|\t\t\t\t\t`{\"call_id\":\"call-nested\",\"status\":\"ok\"}`),\n126|\t\t\t)},\n127|\t\t}\n128|\t\tcapture, store := captureMembers(t, members)\n129|\t\trequest := normalizeRequest(t, capture, store, openTestStore(t))\n130|\t\trequest.Actors = map[string]string{\"subagent:fetch\": fixtureSubActor}\n131|\t\tresolved, err := Normalize(request)\n132|\t\tif err != nil {\n133|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"Normalize() error = %v\", err)\n134|\t\t}\n135|\t\tif len(resolved.ToolResolutions) != 1 || resolved.ToolResolutions[0].Status != \"completed\" {\n136|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"ToolResolutions = %+v, want one completed\", resolved.ToolResolutions)\n137|\t\t}\n138|\t\tcallEvent := eventByNativeID(t, resolved, \"evt-nested-call\")\n139|\t\tif callEvent.Kind != \"tool_call\" {\n140|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"Kind = %q, want tool_call\", callEvent.Kind)\n141|\t\t}\n142|\t\tif callEvent.ActorID.String() != fixtureSubActor {\n143|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"ActorID = %q, want the subagent actor %q\", callEvent.ActorID.String(), fixtureSubActor)\n144|\t\t}\n145|\t\tif callEvent.ActorID.String() == fixtureMainActor {\n146|\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"nested call was attributed to main instead of the subagent actor\")\n147|\t\t}\n148|\t\tsession := resolved.DecodedSession\n149|\t\tif len(session.Actors) != 2 {\n150|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"len(Actors) = %d, want main plus the subagent\", len(session.Actors))\n151|\t\t}\n152|\t\tsubagent := session.Actors[1]\n153|\t\tif subagent.Kind != \"subagent\" {\n154|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"Actors[1].Kind = %q, want subagent\", subagent.Kind)\n155|\t\t}\n156|\t\tif subagent.ParentActorID == nil || subagent.ParentActorID.String() != fixtureMainActor {\n157|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"subagent parent = %v, want main %q\", subagent.ParentActorID, fixtureMainActor)\n158|\t\t}\n159|\t\tif len(resolved.Live.CallableTools) != 0 || len(resolved.Live.PendingActions) != 0 {\n160|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"Live = %+v, want empty\", resolved.Live)\n161|\t\t}\n162|\t})\n163|}\n164|\n165|func TestNormalizeResultAfterBoundaryCompletes(t *testing.T) {\n166|\tcallLine := rec(\"evt-b-call\", \"tool/call\", \"native\", \"none\", \"main\", `{\"call_id\":\"call-b\",\"tool_name\":\"write\"}`)\n167|\tresultLine := rec(\"evt-b-result\", \"tool/result\", \"native\", \"none\", \"main\", `{\"call_id\":\"call-b\",\"status\":\"ok\"}`)\n168|\t// First capture: the call crossed the boundary, the result has\n169|\t// not arrived yet.\n170|\tearly := projectMembers(t, []fixtureMember{\n171|\t\t{key: \"store/session.jsonl\", class: \"durable_payload\", content: jsonl(callLine)},\n172|\t})\n173|\tif len(early.result.ToolResolutions) != 1 || early.result.ToolResolutions[0].Status != \"aborted\" {\n174|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"early ToolResolutions = %+v, want one aborted\", early.result.ToolResolutions)\n175|\t}\n176|\t// Second capture over the later store: the result arrived, the\n177|\t// same call resolves completed.\n178|\tlate := projectMembers(t, []fixtureMember{\n179|\t\t{key: \"store/session.jsonl\", class: \"durable_payload\", content: jsonl(callLine, resultLine)},\n180|\t})\n181|\tif len(late.result.ToolResolutions) != 1 || late.result.ToolResolutions[0].Status != \"completed\" {\n182|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"late ToolResolutions = %+v, want one completed\", late.result.ToolResolutions)\n183|\t}\n184|\tlateCall := eventByNativeID(t, late.result, \"evt-b-call\")\n185|\tif payloadText(t, lateCall, \"resolution\") != \"completed\" {\n186|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"late payload resolution = %q, want completed\", payloadText(t, lateCall, \"resolution\"))\n187|\t}\n188|\tif len(late.result.Live.PendingActions) != 0 {\n189|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"late PendingActions = %q, want empty\", late.result.Live.PendingActions)\n190|\t}\n191|}\n192|\n193|func TestNormalizeToolDefinitionNeverRegistersCallable(t *testing.T) {\n194|\tdigest := fixtureDigest(\"definition-bytes\")\n195|\tbundle := projectMembers(t, []fixtureMember{\n196|\t\t{key: \"store/session.jsonl\", class: \"durable_payload\", content: jsonl(\n197|\t\t\trec(\"evt-def-1\", \"tool/definition\", \"native\", \"none\", \"main\",\n198|\t\t\t\t`{\"tool_name\":\"write\",\"definition_digest\":\"`+digest+`\"}`),\n199|\t\t)},\n200|\t})\n201|\tevent := eventByNativeID(t, bundle.result, \"evt-def-1\")\n202|\tif event.Kind != \"tool_definition_snapshot\" {\n203|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"Kind = %q, want tool_definition_snapshot\", event.Kind)\n204|\t}\n205|\tif event.Visibility != \"internal\" {\n206|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"Visibility = %q, want internal\", event.Visibility)\n207|\t}\n208|\tif payloadBool(t, event, \"callable\") {\n209|\t\tt.Fatal(\"payload callable is true: history registered a callable tool\")\n210|\t}\n211|\tif payloadText(t, event, \"tool_name\") != \"write\" {\n212|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"payload tool_name = %q, want write\", payloadText(t, event, \"tool_name\"))\n213|\t}\n214|\tif len(bundle.result.Live.CallableTools) != 0 {\n215|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"CallableTools = %q, want empty\", bundle.result.Live.CallableTools)\n216|\t}\n217|}\n218|\n219|func TestNormalizeProtectedToolCallStaysOpaqueHistory(t *testing.T) {\n220|\t// A protected tool/call never folds into pairing: it projects\n221|\t// opaque_event while its unprotected result becomes an aborted\n222|\t// orphan. The live surface stays empty.\n223|\tbundle := projectMembers(t, []fixtureMember{\n224|\t\t{key: \"store/session.jsonl\", class: \"durable_payload\", content: jsonl(\n225|\t\t\trec(\"evt-prot-call\", \"tool/call\", \"foreign\", \"encrypted\", \"main\", `{\"ciphertext\":\"x\"}`),\n226|\t\t\trec(\"evt-prot-result\", \"tool/result\", \"native\", \"none\", \"main\", `{\"call_id\":\"c1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}`),\n227|\t\t)},\n228|\t})\n229|\tresolved := bundle.result\n230|\tcallEvent := eventByNativeID(t, resolved, \"evt-prot-call\")\n231|\tif callEvent.Kind != \"opaque_event\" {\n232|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"Kind = %q, want opaque_event: protected call reached a semantic kind\", callEvent.Kind)\n233|\t}\n234|\tif callEvent.Visibility != \"opaque\" {\n235|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"Visibility = %q, want opaque\", callEvent.Visibility)\n236|\t}\n237|\tif len(resolved.ToolResolutions) != 1 || resolved.ToolResolutions[0].Status != \"aborted\" {\n238|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"ToolResolutions = %+v, want one aborted orphan\", resolved.ToolResolutions)\n239|\t}\n240|\torphan := eventByNativeID(t, resolved, \"evt-prot-result\")\n241|\tif orphan.Kind != \"tool_result\" {\n242|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"Kind = %q, want tool_result\", orphan.Kind)\n243|\t}\n244|\tif payloadText(t, orphan, \"resolution\") != \"aborted\" {\n245|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"payload resolution = %q, want aborted\", payloadText(t, orphan, \"resolution\"))\n246|\t}\n247|\tif len(orphan.Evidence.ReasonCodes) != 1 || orphan.Evidence.ReasonCodes[0] != \"unsafe_pending_action\" {\n248|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"ReasonCodes = %q, want [unsafe_pending_action]\", orphan.Evidence.ReasonCodes)\n249|\t}\n250|\tif len(resolved.Live.CallableTools) != 0 || len(resolved.Live.PendingActions) != 0 {\n251|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"Live = %+v, want empty\", resolved.Live)\n252|\t}\n253|}\n254|\n255|func TestNormalizeLiveSurfaceStaysEmpty(t *testing.T) {\n256|\tbundle := projectMembers(t, []fixtureMember{\n257|\t\t{key: \"store/session.jsonl\", class: \"durable_payload\", content: jsonl(\n258|\t\t\trec(\"evt-ls-def\", \"tool/definition\", \"native\", \"none\", \"main\",\n259|\t\t\t\t`{\"tool_name\":\"write\",\"definition_digest\":\"`+fixtureDigest(\"ls-def\")+`\"}`),\n260|\t\t\trec(\"evt-ls-call\", \"tool/call\", \"native\", \"none\", \"main\", `{\"call_id\":\"call-ls\",\"tool_name\":\"write\"}`),\n261|\t\t\trec(\"evt-ls-result\", \"tool/result\", \"native\", \"none\", \"main\", `{\"call_id\":\"call-ls\",\"status\":\"ok\"}`),\n262|\t\t\trec(\"evt-ls-dangling\", \"tool/call\", \"native\", \"none\", \"main\", `{\"call_id\":\"call-dangling\",\"tool_name\":\"read\"}`),\n263|\t\t\trec(\"evt-ls-orphan\", \"tool/result\", \"native\", \"none\", \"main\", `{\"call_id\":\"call-lost\",\"status\":\"error\"}`),\n264|\t\t)},\n265|\t})\n266|\tlive := bundle.result.Live\n267|\tif len(live.CallableTools) != 0 {\n268|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"CallableTools = %q, want empty\", live.CallableTools)\n269|\t}\n270|\tif len(live.PendingActions) != 0 {\n271|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"PendingActions = %q, want empty\", live.PendingActions)\n272|\t}\n273|\tif len(bundle.result.ToolResolutions) != 3 {\n274|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"len(ToolResolutions) = %d, want 3 (completed, aborted, orphan)\", len(bundle.result.ToolResolutions))\n275|\t}\n276|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
