pe; record lives in the three TRACEABILITY files + matrices). Pin tests updated (report wants, sliver tables, 10.2 rename row now attacks `Capture`, admits lists extended to 7.8/10.2, README figure pins with `twelve`/`forty-seven`); README package section + measured-coverage rewrite (fenced line byte-equal).\\n- REFRESH: this run opened on stale base `a12d1bd` (branch tip `47294bb`) while trunk was `c3aae73`, so `refresh-candidate` ran FIRST (`refresh_advanced` onto `c3aae73`, checkpoint-bound LOGBOOK replay keeping trunk's 4qojoz entry newest-first). The audit restored trunk bytes for every carried stale revert (`.task-board`, `internal/meshneg`, `internal/rpcwire` tests/harness, `internal/matjournal` test, `task-board.config.json` back to the 30-command form); README/LOGBOOK/traceability edits were re-applied purely additively on the new bytes and the ownership registry MERGED (trunk's 5 cases + 3 upgraded bindings kept, this story's 4 cases + 2 bindings appended/transplanted — never replaced). Full 30-command suite green on the refreshed tree (race gate in 7 bounded groups incl. sessquery alone, 41/41 packages, no DATA RACE).\\n- BOUNDS (sibling scope, not waived): fixture-native record envelope is test-defined framing (body shapes exact, envelope extras unclaimed); fact registries only for emitted kinds; native-protected records carry no reason code; turn IDs/source times null; call arguments not carried; SYNTHESIZED/partial/unavailable statuses and non-text content blocks never emitted (shape rules owned by the accepted clonebundle suite); 13.14.2–13.14.5 (fidelity dispositions, planning, lineage, transaction, tuple admission) sibling-owned; 7.8 operation frames stay `sessadapter`. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\\n- AC: 24 of 24 rows driven through `Normalize` by named tests and measured with narrowings (matrix in `TASK-260830-32ypr2_conformance-matrix.md`).\\n- REV2 (rework of review RUN-260918-320878, CHANGES REQUESTED; no base move, still `3005d78` over trunk `c3aae73`): P1-a CLOSED — envelope+body frame decodes delegate to `environ.DecodeStrictObject` at `strictMembers` (lone-surrogate/duplicate/trailing faults refuse with the fault named; the later struct read is exact because the rewriting/guessing shapes never pass the gate); 4 new refusal rows + 4 narrowings. P2-c CLOSED — `bodyUint53` and the envelope version delegate to `environ.CheckUint53Bounds` (string-typed numbers refuse; per-member failures merge into one \\\"is not a uint53\\\" refusal while the ledger sum keeps \\\"exceeds uint53\\\"); string rows + 5 narrowings. New P3 rows: actor-order determinism (3 actors x12, `N-actors-sort`), both type/protection agreement arms, trailing bytes, protected-tool fold-skip, result-status vocabulary, size arm with its own message + drift row, unknown+protected body refusal; P3-i non-JSONL bound stated + pinned, P3-l null-directives pinned, P3-c per-edge rows stated as bounds (the \\\"representative\\\" claim removed); P3-j unions the 10.2 binding to 11 cases (10.2#2 gains `localstore-immutable-blob-install`); P3-k relabels (`N-empty-projection` single-member class, `N-overflow-truncate` behaviour swap). P2-a: one decision line per inherited advisory group (1,2,3,5,6,7b deferred with owners; 4/P3-e closed as a stated bound; 7a/P3-ζ closed by P1-a; 7c/P3-ζ′ rewritten as a deferred-unification bound) and the two false-prose sites rewritten. P2-b: 7.8#1 rebound to the new `session-adapter-frame-bound` case (`DecodeRequestFrame` + the oversize/edge tests, sessadapter owner); cases 144→145; digest re-derived `4bd01143…` gate-computed; README prose fixed (7.8 bound to sessadapter, Nine cases, admissions list, 10.2 union note).\\n- REV2 EVIDENCE: 62 narrowing + 2 labelled rows KILLED + control SURVIVED, battery green twice with per-plant raw logs; the six re-anchorable reviewer plants (R1,R2,R5,R6,R7,R8 shapes) KILLED firsthand by the new tests. AC: 38 of 38 rows driven through `Normalize` by named tests (matrix rev2).\\n\\n### STORY-260830-4qojoz (mesh-rpc-framing-and-negotiation) — final leaf TASK-260830-19bjfj rev2: adversarial closure on the adopted v0.7.0 registry\\n- REWORK (test-only; no production behavior file changed): rev1 was reviewed CHANGES REQUESTED on the story-close half only — its technical body (N1-N3 closure, mutants, fuzz controls, 23/29 AC ratio) was independently reproduced by the reviewer. Rev1 was built on stale base 888ae3d while trunk adopted v0.7.0 (2fc6d50) mid-run. Rev2 refreshed the candidate onto 2fc6d50 (`refresh_advanced`, checkpoint-bound LOGBOOK replay: trunk's two v0.7.0 entries kept newest-first, 219okr block carried verbatim below them) and re-based every story-close edit on trunk bytes.\\n- TRACEABILITY: registry work moved into adopted `ownership.v0.7.0.json` (5 new acceptance cases, 3 upgraded bindings: 11.2 partial 3/5, 17.1 partial 3/6, 17.4 sliver 1/4); every clause line re-measured against the pinned v0.7.0 document through the production clause inventory (11.2: 7364/7408/7420; 17.1: 15567/15589/15602; 17.4: 15661). The invented 11.3#18 binding is dropped — no production code parses a digest-identity array, so 11.3 stays the carried unevidenced stub and `rpcwire-inventory-arrays` was not ported. Digest re-derived `b4ae9091…` (gate-computed, shown in results). tracecheck green `56/569` (+7); section runs refuse admission with the measured ratios, quoted verbatim. Deliberate pins: `traceability_test.go`/`main_test.go` figure tables, the README pin test's closed number-word map extended with `eight`/`forty-nine`, and a reviewed-upgrade extension to `TestV070RegistryRederivesFromTrunkV060Registry` (each upgraded binding/case pinned literally, new clauses re-measured; every other binding still rederives byte-equal).\\n- P3 GAPS (all closed with a failing-without-it test): opaque-body object gate over `health.get` (`[]`/`null`/`\\\"x\\\"`/`42`/duplicate-member → ErrFrame) + `FuzzClosedOperationBodies` now feeds raw bodies with an I-JSON object oracle (the naive `&& op !=` plant is vacuous — the stale `err` still propagates — so the committed probe restructures the gate); changed-body retry after a committed effect → literal `idempotency_mismatch` with a single retained journal (one-off J1 overlay kills the new test, staging still passes); body-fuzzer oracle bound stated explicitly (member-name + object + round-trip only; bounds/vocabularies owned by the unit suite) + hello-body-extra seed in `FuzzUnknownFields`; exact 8388608-admit/8388609-refuse encode edge; `ErrVersionMismatch` class pinned in the error-schema lanes; literal `[2 3 4]`/`[5]` offer sets in the N2 rows; nonce-alphabet plant widened to the full unpadded standard-base64 class (two-arm `RawStdEncoding` narrowing, no new import).\\n- MUTANTS: meshneg 37 killed / neutral passed / detail-text SURVIVED (exit 0); rpcwire 41 killed / neutral passed / error-text SURVIVED (exit 0). Fuzz controls re-run on the new targets: all three FAIL on their plants (exit 1) plus the two new P3 control proofs. Full 30-command suite green on the refreshed tree (race gate in 5 chunks, sessquery alone; no DATA RACE). Per-plant raw logs + tables in the outcome tar; `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`.\\n- BOUNDS (stated, not green): 22/24 op bodies opaque; no minor-selection entry; envelope request_id correlation-only (replay/idempotency adopted from matjournal plus the new committed-phase pin); chunk-data base64 unwitnessed (strictness pinned at the nonce gate); RPC layer mutates nothing (purity bound). AC: 23 of 29 rows driven through production entries by named tests, 6 declared stated bounds (matrix in the outcome evidence).\\n- Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree for handoff snapshot; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2g5be6 — native capture and source-race check (second leaf)\\n\\n- DELIVERED: `internal/clonesnap` implements the Section 13.14.1 capture operation over a real fixture store — contained walk (`secprim` Guard opens, symlink-intermediate/FIFO/dir refusals naming the member), nine-class classification with always-excluded bytes never opened, Capture Boundary from measured evidence (stable proof or core-created `unstable_archive`), a source-race gate comparing content digests before any seal, workspace checkpoint + source head from observed state, Section 10.2 descriptors (empty/multi-chunk) with `capability_unavailable` past 128 GiB, and target admission (`RefuseUnstableForTarget`, `RefuseMaximalSafeUnlessComplete`) emitting an admission receipt. Every manifest seals through the landed `clonebundle` builders and re-decodes before publish; every byte installs through `localstore` no-replace.\\n- ORDERING (the task's named check): the sealed stable proof carries the two measured source digests (pre and post) — the gate proved them equal before the seal ran, so the sealed bytes equal either measurement — and the ordering mutants prove the gate precedes the seal at both entries: `N-race-order-capture` (manifest scan), `N-race-order-project` (seal error message), `N-race-order-project-seal` (capture-store scan at the projection entry). Changed byte/size, appended record, replaced/removed file, excluded size change, and unreadable-at-post each refuse or seal `unstable_archive` with `source_not_quiescent`, never silently stable.\\n- EVIDENCE: package suite green (positives, full refusal table, 4-class leak scan over blobs/manifests/logs/errors, digest-only log assertions, every-payload-blob-installed assertion after Capture and after the crash replay, target-sink-empty assertion on the archive path, real-SIGKILL crash test with replay convergence + clean-run byte equality, idempotent triple-project); 41 narrowing + 2 add-write rows KILLED + harmless control SURVIVED (`testdata/mutant_harness.py --log-dir`, one raw log per plant with subprocess exit, `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`), including the token-preserving prefix mutant killed by the behavioral Capture entry and the cross-package P3-ε row (plant in clonebundle, killer here). No `internal/traceability` edit (FINAL leaf carries bindings + re-pin); clause map in `internal/clonesnap/TRACEABILITY.md`.\\n- REV3 (rework of review RUN-260918-fdce92; no base move, still `2f844bb` over trunk `a12d1bd`; `origin/main` still `c3aae73`): row 8 sealed unstable pre/post digests + generation asserted against the measurements (`N-unstable-seals-pre-as-post`); row 10 capture-store manifest scan at `CaptureAndProject` (`N-race-order-project-seal`, killed by the scan — `N-race-order-project` is killed by the seal error message); P3-a unplanned-symlink row, P3-b symlinked-store-root row, P3-c excluded-size row (shipped, not reworded); P3-d branch bound attributed to the landed `DecodeWorkspaceBinding` with a first-hand survival probe; P3-e four rows shipped (plan grammar, required blockedAncestor, fingerprints-129, first-chunk-oversize). Only production edit is the ORDER-PIN comment (inert receipt clause fixed).\\n- INHERITED (rev2 rework): P3-ε CLOSED here (excluded unknown drives `raw_complete=false` and blocks `maximal_safe` at this leaf's projection entry, test + cross-package harness row); P3-ζ DEFERRED to TASK-260830-32ypr2 (no title/text admission site in this leaf); P3-η PARTIAL — this leaf's entry re-validation pinned by test, the standalone `EncodeNativeIdentity` contract deferred to the clonebundle owner or the final leaf. P3-γ sealed the measured post digest; P3-δ reworded as defence-in-depth; P3-ε′ orphan-blob row shipped; P3-ζ′ fidelity duplication recorded as a bound.\\n- BOUNDS (sibling scope, not waived): no `ax` CLI/provider process/network (fixture store); Section 7.8 operation wiring stays `sessadapter`; projection planning past admission is the final leaf's; excluded-byte equal-size changes are below the detection floor (never opened by design); sub-walk transient swaps restored before post-measure are below the floor (no fs snapshot). Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\\n- AC: 17 of 17 rows driven through production entries by named tests and measured at the member level — every row's narrowing reddens its killer (matrix in `TASK-260830-2g5be6_conformance-matrix.md`).\\n\\n## 2026-09-17\\n\\n### TASK-260830-24z2b3 — clone bundle + canonical session/event types (first leaf)\\n\\n- DELIVERED: `internal/clonebundle` implements the Section 13.14.1 capture contracts over the landed owners — Clone Raw Object Manifest 1.0.0, Clone Capture Manifest 1.0.0 (Capture Items, Source Basis, Capture Boundary, core-derived `raw_complete`), Canonical Session 1.0.0 + Actors, Canonical Event 1.0.0 (Source Evidence, raw refs, content blocks), NativeIdentity/WorkspaceBinding, immutable generations — plus Section 10.2 descriptor agreement and no-replace install via `localstore`. Every Build entry is byte-identical for identical inputs; every Decode entry enforces the closed shape. Row-21 exclusion allowlist (`hosttrust` matchers) enforced at raw-entry and capture-item construction with per-class negatives.\\n- OWNERSHIP: `canonicaljson` keeps its `rejectUnsupportedImmutableObjectShape` rows (that table's census pins every row); this package is the validating owner and reuses `Canonicalize` (byte transform), `CalculateObjectIdentity` plus local claim comparisons (blobs; never the attesting `VerifyObjectIdentity` entry — only the test fixture calls it — per the provhost no-attestation bound), `sessadapter.DecodeTuple`, the `environ` scalar gate set via delegating wrappers, `scalar`, `hosttrust`, and `localstore.PutBlob`. No `internal/traceability` edit (FINAL leaf carries bindings + re-pin); clause map in `internal/clonebundle/TRACEABILITY.md`.\\n- EVIDENCE: package suite green (87.1% statements), 66 narrowing mutants KILLED + harmless control SURVIVED (`testdata/mutant_harness.py --log-dir`, one raw log per plant with subprocess exit, `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`); `TestInstallRawBlobIsIdempotent` + `Test