{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d09f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b42c-6247-7d31-b9d8-d87c5b1f64f4"},"sequence":1706,"recorded_at":1780531400003407,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"0dc60d48-0449-4263-a4d2-db59edd40fb4","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"0dc60d48-0449-4263-a4d2-db59edd40fb4","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"0dc60d48-0449-4263-a4d2-db59edd40fb4"},"call_id":"call_01a0b439d7ed7272ad8e8e0643848214","text":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 125-137\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-`testdata/mutant_harness.py` ships 62 narrowing rows, 2 labelled\n-non-narrowing rows, and the harmless `C-doc-comment` SURVIVED\n-control. Every narrowing weakens one gate to admit exactly one\n-member of the class it must reject, and every killer drives the\n-production `Normalize` entry over real captured bytes.\n-`N-native-type-token` and `N-protection-encrypted` are the\n-token-preserving attacks: the searched-for text still matches\n-while the decision changes, and the killers execute the\n-behavioral suite. `N-empty-projection` is labelled single-member\n-class and `N-overflow-truncate` is labelled behaviour swap; no\n-other row is an arm-delete, and no plant covers two sites. The\n-battery runs twice with one raw log per plant per run carrying\n-the subprocess exit.\n+`testdata/mutant_harness.py` ships 72 narrowing rows, 3 labelled\n+non-narrowing rows, and the harmless `C-doc-comment` SURVIVED\n+control. Every narrowing weakens one gate to admit exactly one\n+member of the class it must reject, and every killer drives the\n+production `Normalize` entry over real captured bytes.\n+`N-native-type-token` and `N-protection-encrypted` are the\n+token-preserving attacks: the searched-for text still matches\n+while the decision changes, and the killers execute the\n+behavioral suite. The six `N-alias-*` rows restore the\n+case-folded read for exactly one envelope member each; every\n+other alias stays an unclaimed extra under the plant.\n+`N-empty-projection` is labelled single-member class,\n+`N-overflow-truncate` is labelled behaviour swap, and\n+`N-pending-aborted` is labelled add-arm (`Normalize` passes nil\n+live work orders, so the narrowed condition alone cannot pend\n+from the entry and the plant appends the call explicitly); no\n+other row is an arm-delete. The five `N-strict-*` rows patch the\n+shared `strictMembers` body used by both frame sites (one gate,\n+two call sites); every other plant patches one site. The battery\n+runs twice with one raw log per plant per run carrying the\n+subprocess exit.\n","edit_facts":{"tool_name":"edit_file","path":"internal/cloneproject/TRACEABILITY.md","added":21,"removed":13},"correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"edit_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d0a1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b42c-6247-7d31-b9d8-d87c5b1f64f4"},"sequence":1707,"recorded_at":1780531400003409,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"0dc60d48-0449-4263-a4d2-db59edd40fb4","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"0dc60d48-0449-4263-a4d2-db59edd40fb4","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"0dc60d48-0449-4263-a4d2-db59edd40fb4"},"call_id":"call_01a0b439e6de72c9bb6e700e97f905ff","text":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 171-177\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-- Per-edge character-width rows past the envelope ID edge\n-  (directive 4096/4097, call ID 512/513, tool names) are stated\n-  bounds: every edge checks through the landed\n-  `environ.StringLength` gate, but only the envelope ID edge\n-  carries a narrowing (`N-string-bound`).\n-- `\"directives\":null` decodes as zero directives: null is not\n-  distinguished from an empty array at the instruction body.\n+- Envelope extras are unclaimed and can never override a claimed\n+  member: the envelope is read from the strict map by exact name\n+  with no second decoder, and case-folded aliases are inert\n+  extras in any document order (pinned by\n+  `TestNormalizeCaseAliasEnvelopeIgnoresUnclaimedMembers`, whose\n+  control subtest keeps an unrelated extra admitted).\n+- Per-edge character-width rows past the envelope ID edge\n+  (native_type 512/513, directive 4096/4097, call ID 512/513,\n+  tool names) are stated bounds: every edge checks through the\n+  landed `environ.StringLength` gate, but only the envelope ID\n+  edge carries a narrowing (`N-string-bound`).\n+- `\"directives\":null` decodes as zero directives: null is not\n+  distinguished from an empty array at the instruction body.\n+- `\"text\":null` seals as empty inline content (pinned by\n+  `TestNormalizeNullTextDecodesAsEmpty`); `\"ciphertext\":null`\n+  is admitted but harmless (the value is never read, only the\n+  protected shape is checked).\n","edit_facts":{"tool_name":"edit_file","path":"internal/cloneproject/TRACEABILITY.md","added":17,"removed":7},"correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"edit_file","outcome":"success"}}}
