{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d119","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b42c-6247-7d31-b9d8-d87c5b1f64f4"},"sequence":1767,"recorded_at":1780531400003529,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"0dc60d48-0449-4263-a4d2-db59edd40fb4","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"0dc60d48-0449-4263-a4d2-db59edd40fb4","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"0dc60d48-0449-4263-a4d2-db59edd40fb4"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b43a-701d-7a10-acb3-e2336e732422"},"task_id":"01a0b43a-701d-7a10-acb3-e2336e732422","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b43a-701d-7a10-acb3-e2336e732422","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: line 17\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-- REV2 EVIDENCE: 62 narrowing + 2 labelled rows KILLED + control SURVIVED, battery green twice with per-plant raw logs; the six re-anchorable reviewer plants (R1,R2,R5,R6,R7,R8 shapes) KILLED firsthand by the new tests. AC: 38 of 38 rows driven through `Normalize` by named tests (matrix rev2).\n+- REV2 EVIDENCE: 62 narrowing + 2 labelled rows KILLED + control SURVIVED, battery green twice with per-plant raw logs; the six re-anchorable reviewer plants (R1,R2,R5,R6,R7,R8 shapes) KILLED firsthand by the new tests. AC: 38 of 38 rows driven through `Normalize` by named tests (matrix rev2).\n+- REV3 CORRECTION (rework of review RUN-260918-a4ffef, CHANGES REQUESTED; no base move, still `3005d78` over trunk `c3aae73`): the REV2 sentence \"the later struct read is exact because the rewriting/guessing shapes never pass the gate\" was FALSE — the struct decode matched member names case-insensitively and took the last match, so a case-folded alias overrode the claimed value while the strict map admitted it as a distinct extra. The second decoder is DELETED: `parseNativeLine` now reads the six claimed envelope members from the strict map by exact name (`json.Unmarshal(members[name], ...)` + `Body = members[\"body\"]`), and no lenient re-read of the envelope remains anywhere after the strict gate (verified by grep: the only struct decode is gone; every other `Unmarshal` reads a strict-map member or a sealed manifest map by exact key).\n+- REV3 (same run): P1-b CLOSED — `TestNormalizeCaseAliasEnvelopeIgnoresUnclaimedMembers` pins all six alias axes through `Normalize` (kind in both document orders, origin/authority, protection/promotion refusal, body/content, evidence identity, actor/attribution refusal) plus an unrelated-extra control; six `N-alias-*` narrowings each restore the case-folded read for exactly one member and all KILLED. P2-d CLOSED — positive `reasoning_summary` row (`TestNormalizeReasoningSummaryProjectsInternal`) + routing-swap narrowing. P3-m capture status asserted for every emitted kind (`TestNormalizeCaptureStatusExactForEveryKind` + partial-stamp narrowing); P3-n last-wins pinned by two native instructions (`TestNormalizeLastNativeInstructionWins` + fold-first narrowing); P3-o external kind pinned (`TestNormalizeExternalActorSealsAsExternal` + kind narrowing, and the reviewer-exact R7 swap KILLED firsthand); P3-p unknown-type-without-body refusal row + required-member narrowing (reviewer R1 shape); P3-q `text:null` stated as a bound (seals empty inline content, pinned) with `ciphertext:null` noted harmless; P3-r `N-pending-aborted` relabelled add-arm and the shared-site `N-strict-*` rows disclosed as one gate/two call sites (harness + TRACEABILITY + matrix + results); P3-s per-edge bound text now names `native_type` (reviewer R2 re-run firsthand: SURVIVED, inside the bound). Five prose sites corrected (`native.go` comments, TRACEABILITY rows, README exact-name sentence, this entry, results).\n+- REV3 EVIDENCE: 72 narrowing + 3 labelled rows KILLED + control SURVIVED, battery green twice with per-plant raw logs; reviewer R1/R4/R5/R6 shapes adopted as shipped narrowings, R7 adopted as a condition narrowing with the exact swap also KILLED firsthand, R3 still KILLED (untouched line). AC: 45 of 45 rows driven through `Normalize` by named tests (matrix rev3).\n","final_result":true}}}
